{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5434357/patrol-officer": {
      "title": "Patrol Officer",
      "description": "Patrol Officer Salary $50,011.00 Annually Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02561 Division Administration and Finance Department University Police/Public Safety Opening Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date Continuous Reference Number AF 2026-23 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description POSITION SUMMARY: Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applicants to a for a full-time Patrol Officer in the Public Safety Department. Join the IUP community as a Patrol Officer, where your role goes beyond traditional policing. You'll engage with students, faculty and staff fostering a safe and welcoming environment on campus. Enjoy a diverse and dynamic setting, where every day presents new challenges and opportunities to make a positive impact. University Patrol Officers are responsible for providing a safe and secure living and learning environment for the University Community. Officers are on duty 365 days a year and provide immediate responses to all types of emergencies on campus while providing services in areas of patrol, investigations, parking enforcement, residence hall protection, building security, crime prevention and special event security. This position involves a great deal of interaction with students, performing community-oriented policing with a strong emphasis on student success and retention, recognizing the social importance of 21 st Century professional and ethical police functions for tactful and courteous treatment of all persons. This is an “essential personnel” position. Patrol officers are expected to remain or report to work during partial or full day closings and during other emergent circumstances. ESSENTIAL DUTIES: Patrol campus property and buildings by foot, vehicle, or bike to ensure proper security and safety; including but not limited to locking, and unlocking of facilities; precluding theft, vandalism, and loitering; reporting of general building and grounds security issues; building checks for safety hazards, mechanical problems and failures and other deficiencies. Direct and control traffic and parking on University grounds: Issuing traffic warnings, parking tickets, and traffic and non-traffic citations, for violations of University policy and Commonwealth of Pennsylvania laws. Investigate traffic accidents involving persons or property, report and pursue appropriate course of action on university grounds. Display and remove temporary parking signage on campus. Provide safety and law enforcement for extra-curricular, social, recreational, and free assembly events/activities at the University. Operate state vehicles in a legal, safe, and courteous manner. Provide transportation, with the use of a state-owned vehicle, for persons to and from hospitals, university funds or valuables to proper locations, prisoners, and legal documents for service of process. Respond to non-emergency calls for assistance (criminal and general assistance). Respond to emergency calls, including but not limited to mental health, injured persons, panic, fire, burglary alarms, bomb threat, active assailant, or any other University emergency. Investigate suspected crimes, report findings, file criminal complaints, serve arrest and search warrants, and/or conduct surveillance while following Rules of Criminal Procedure & University Police policies. Testify in court, legal proceedings, or university code of conduct hearings as necessary. Aid other local law enforcement agencies in the direction of the senior officer in charge. Prepare and maintain a multitude of reports; daily activity logs, shift reports etc. to department standards. Utilizes two-way radio communication equipment, computers, multi-line telephones, monitor alarms & CCTV. Accomplish routine administrative duties and perform other related work as required. Participate in education and training courses, as requested. Complete professional development training as required (CPR/AED, firearms, Act 180 etc.) Practice safety measures to prevent accidents and injuries, and to ensure compliance with applicable regulations. Complete reports to appropriate work group of deficiencies. Perform public speaking-community policing events with student or community groups as a special assignment. Exhibit abilities to work with diverse groups and populations. Maintain a high level of confidentiality, CHRIA, FERPA, HIPAA, JNET, CLEAN *The General Summary and Essential Duties and Responsibilities section summarized above provides a representative listing only and should not be regarded as a complete statement of tasks performed by incumbents of this position. It should be recognized, therefore, that employees may be asked to perform job-related duties in addition to those outlined above. IMPORTANT NOTICE: This position posting is to establish a pool of qualified candidates for anticipated future full-time Patrol Officer openings in the Public Safety Department. While there may not be an immediate vacancy, applications submitted to this pool will be reviewed as full-time positions become available. The posting will remain open until a successful candidate is selected. Position Qualifications REQUIRED KNOWLEDGES, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Knowledge of Commonwealth laws, rules, and regulations governing motor vehicle operation and personal conduct for employees or visitors at Commonwealth facilities Knowledge of Commonwealth provisions for emergency situations Some knowledge of group behavior Skill in the use and care of offensive and defensive weapons Ability to react quickly and calmly in emergency situations and to determine proper courses of action Ability to enforce laws firmly, tactfully, and with respect for the rights of others. Ability to understand and carry out oral and written instructions MINIMUM EXPERIENCE AND TRAINING: One year of police experience and formal training in the provisions of basic police services as certified through Act 120 training; OR Any equivalent experience or training. NECESSARY SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS: Possession of a valid Pennsylvania Driver's license. Ability to meet such qualifications regarding strength, agility, and health as required. Receipt of the MPOETC Certification with arrest powers, granted by the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Successfully complete the University Firearms Qualification Requirements at required intervals. Satisfactorily complete Act 180 updates annually. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for SPFPA employees, please click on the link below: http://www.passhe.edu/inside/HR/syshr/benefit_highlights/SSHE_Highlights.pdf 01 Do you have one year of police experience and formal training in the provisions of basic police services as certified through Act 120 training or any equivalent of experience or training? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5463759/patrol-officer-trainee": {
      "title": "Patrol Officer Trainee",
      "description": "Patrol Officer Trainee Salary $17.56 Hourly Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02590 Division Administration and Finance Department Police/Dispatch Opening Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date Continuous Reference Number AF 2026-** Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description POSITION SUMMARY: Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applicants for a Patrol Officer Trainee in t he Department of Public Safety and Police. The Patrol Officer trainee position is an entry-level position designed to identify new police recruits. An employee in this job participates in an MPOETC Certified Act 120 program. An employee in this job develops skills and techniques to provide police services and protection to the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education property, grounds, facilities, clientele, employees, and the general public. Work involves learning to enforce the Pennsylvania Crimes Code, Motor Vehicle Code, local ordinances, and commonwealth regulations. Assignments are designed to develop proficiency in law interpretation and application, legal procedures, police operations, criminal investigations, public safety, physical fitness, self-defense, firearms use, emergency response, effective communication, report writing, maintenance and use of equipment, and law enforcement practices. Work may also include performing on-the-job assignments patrolling a State University to protect and guard property or persons from fire, theft, trespass, or other hazards. Performance is evaluated in accordance with prescribed regulations and procedures, formal inspections, personal observation, and successful completion of an MPOETC Certified Act 120 program. The officer trainee will never betray their integrity, character, or the public trust. The officer trainee will treat all individuals with dignity and respect and ensure their actions are dedicated to ensuring the safety of my community and the preservation of human life. Trainees will always have the courage to hold themself and others accountable for our actions. Trainees will maintain the highest ethical standards and uphold the values of the University and police department they serve. ESSENTIAL DUTIES: Participate in a structured Act 120 Basic Police Officer Training program to obtain Act 120 Certification. Participate in training assignments to learn the principles and practices associated with conducting investigations, collecting evidence to support enforcement action, search and seizure, accident investigations, officer safety, interpersonal relations, investigations, interviews, interrogations, report writing, case preparation, and court testimony. Receive training in the safe and proper handling of firearms and in the use of specialized equipment and instruments, including communications equipment, preliminary breath test devices, body armor, and riot gear. Participate in training assignments to learn the principles and practices associated with the Rules of Criminal Procedure, the Rules of Evidence, criminal laws, motor vehicle laws, and rules related to search and seizure and arrest. Patrol an assigned area of the university, watches for fires, prowlers, vandalism, or other unusual occurrences. Direct traffic and enforce parking regulations. Assist and direct visitors; furnish information in a courteous manner. Maintain orderly conduct among students, employees, visitors, and the general public. Operate motorized vehicles. Perform related work and all other duties as required. IMPORTANT NOTICE: This position posting is to establish a pool of qualified candidates for anticipated future full-time Patrol Officer Trainee openings in the Public Safety Department. While there may not be an immediate vacancy, applications submitted to this pool will be reviewed as full-time positions become available. The posting will remain open until a successful candidate is selected. Position Qualifications MINIMUM EXPERIENCE AND TRAINING: High school Diploma or completion of the General Educational Development test. Must possess a valid driver's license. Special Instructions to Applicants All positions require possession of an active motor vehicle operator’s license. All employees must meet the entrance requirements for the MPOETC Certified Act 120 program which includes a fitness test, a background check, a physical examination including a vision and hearing test, a psychological examination, and a reading test with a minimum 9 th grade reading level. All employees are required to enroll in, participate, and complete the Municipal Police Officers’ Education and Training Commission Certified Basic Police Academy (Act 120) training to obtain MPOETC Certification. Act 120 certification must be obtained to successfully complete the trainee program. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. Non-mgmt, non-represented employees 01 Do you have a high school diploma, or have you completed the General Educational Development test? Yes No 02 Do you possess a valid driver's license? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5482577/college-of-osteopathic-medicine-clinical-sciences-faculty": {
      "title": "College of Osteopathic Medicine - Clinical Sciences Faculty",
      "description": "College of Osteopathic Medicine - Clinical Sciences Faculty Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02593 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 09/18/2026 Closing Date 10/19/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number 2026 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The IUP College of Osteopathic Medicine (IUPCOM) invites applicants for several inaugural full-time, tenure track and part-time nontenure track Clinical Sciences faculty teaching positions beginning in the Fall of 2026. These roles offer a distinctive opportunity to contribute to the College’s development by helping to shape a forward-thinking and rurally-focused medical education program grounded in interdisciplinary collaboration, community engagement, and academic excellence with early clinical experiences. Successful candidates will demonstrate a strong and engaged commitment to medical education and play an integral role in delivering an innovative, integrated, systems-based curriculum that prioritizes active learning, clinical relevance, and interprofessional collaboration. IUP is officially classified as an R2 doctoral universityinstitution and the College offers generous start-up financial support, research laboratory space and equipment, and other internal resources/support for scholarly pursuits. The faculty, working closely with the IUPCOM Dean's Office, will provide support for the organization, development, operationalization, and assessment of the clinical aspects of the four-year educational curricular continuum. Note: these roles are curriculum development focused until students matriculate in the fall of 2027, which will then transition into teaching-focus with continued curriculum development. Clinical Faculty Sought We are seeking multiple full-time, tenure track and part-time nontenure track faculty members at the Instructor, Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level. Note: These positions will involve teaching upon commencement of AY 2027-2028. Prior to that, the roles will focus mostly on curriculum development and preparation of the academic program up until the start of AY 2027-2028. These positions include, but are not limited to, the following disciplines/roles: Primary Care (multiple position openings-family medicine, internal medicine, pediatrics) Curriculum development, and once student matriculate, deliver lectures, clinical skills lab instruction, including standardized patients and simulation-based activities; facilitate small-group, team-based, or case-based learning sessions; integrate clinical correlations and osteopathic principles (OMM relevance to anatomy); develop practical exams and written assessments; develop and lead the family medicine, internal medicine, and pediatrics rotations in Year 3; develop and lead the Rural Family Medicine rotation in Year 3, and the internal medicine/pediatrics subspecialty rotation in Year 4; teach general clinical medicine in both the pre-clinical and clinical years, including going out to the clinical sites to work with students in rural areas to train them on how primary care is delivered rurally; work with Clinical Skills and Simulation Faculty to develop cases and learning modalities through years 1-4 with family medicine, internal medicine, and pediatrics input; deliver instruction on primary care in each of the systems where appropriate; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on primary care conditions; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns. OPP/OMM/NMM Department Faculty, multiple positions Develop curriculum and, once students matriculate, teach/lead the OMM/OPP I-VI courses in the four-year curriculum; teach general clinical medicine in both the pre-clinical and clinical years, including going out to the clinical sites to work with students in rural areas to train them on how OPP/NMM care is delivered rurally; work with Clinical Skills and Simulation Faculty to develop cases and learning modalities through years 1-4 with integrated OMM/NMM content; deliver instruction on OPP/NMM in each of the systems where appropriate; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on OPP/NMM conditions; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns. Founding Psychiatry Faculty – Division Chief Develop curriculum and once students matriculate, instruct/lead the Psychiatry System course in Year 2; develop and lead the Psychiatry rotation in Year 3; develop and lead the Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences I-VI four year curriculum; teach general clinical medicine and psychiatry in both the pre-clinical and clinical years, including going out to the clinical sites to work with students in rural areas to train them on how psychiatric care is delivered rurally; work with Clinical Skills and Simulation Faculty to develop cases and learning modalities through years 1-4 with psychiatric input; deliver instruction on psychiatry in each of the systems where appropriate; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on psychiatric conditions; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns. Behavioral Health Specialist Assist in curricular development and once students matriculate, deliver instruction on psychology, psychiatry, social determinants of health, ethics, and professionalism; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); lead sessions on clinical skills such as motivational interviewing, empathy, and cultural competence; connect behavioral health concepts to primary care, chronic disease management, and whole-person osteopathic care; reinforce mind-body-spirit principles central to osteopathic philosophy; design longitudinal behavioral science/psychiatry content across preclinical and sometimes clinical years; develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on psychiatric conditions and behavioral principles; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns; collaborate with social workers, psychologists, and community health organizations; incorporate population health, public health, and health disparities into teaching Pediatrics - Division Chief Develop curriculum and once students matriculate lead the Pediatrics System course once students enrolled in Year 2; develop and lead the Pediatrics rotation in Year 3; teach general clinical medicine in both the pre-clinical and clinical years, including going out to the clinical sites to work with students in rural areas to train them on how pediatric care is delivered rurally; work with Clinical Skills and Simulation Faculty to develop cases and learning modalities through years 1-4 with pediatric input; deliver instruction on pediatrics in each of the systems where appropriate; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on pediatric conditions; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns. Founding OB/GYN Faculty – Division Chief Develop curriculum and once students matriculate teach/lead the OB/GYN System course in Year 2; develop and lead the OB/GYN rotation in Year 3; teach general clinical medicine and OB/GYN related concepts in both the pre-clinical and clinical years, including going out to the clinical sites to work with students in rural areas to train them on how OB/GYN care is delivered rurally; work with Clinical Skills and Simulation Faculty to develop cases and learning modalities through years 1-4 with OB/GYN input; deliver instruction on psychiatry in each of the systems where appropriate; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on OB/GYN conditions; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns. Founding Surgery Faculty – Division Chief Develop curriculum and once students matriculate teach/lead the SURGERY System course in Year 2; develop and lead the SURGERY rotation in Year 3; teach general clinical medicine and SURGERY related concepts in both the pre-clinical and clinical years, including going out to the clinical sites to work with students in rural areas to train them on how SURGERY care is delivered rurally; work with Clinical Skills and Simulation Faculty to develop cases and learning modalities through years 1-4 with SURGERY input; deliver instruction on psychiatry in each of the systems where appropriate; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on SURGERY conditions; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns. Founding Emergency Medicine Faculty – Division Chief Develop curriculum and once students matriculate teach/lead the EMERGENCY MEDICINE System course in Year 2; develop and lead the EMERGENCY MEDICINE rotation in Year 3; teach general clinical medicine and EMERGENCY MEDICINE related concepts in both the pre-clinical and clinical years, including going out to the clinical sites to work with students in rural areas to train them on how EMERGENCY MEDICINE care is delivered rurally; work with Clinical Skills and Simulation Faculty to develop cases and learning modalities through years 1-4 with EMERGENCY MEDICINE input; deliver instruction on psychiatry in each of the systems where appropriate; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on EMERGENCY MEDICINE conditions; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns. Founding Hematology/Oncology Faculty Develop curriculum and once students matriculate lead the Hematology/Oncology System course in Year 1; develop and support the Internal Medicine rotation in Year 3; develop an elective course in Hematology/Oncology for Year 4; teach general clinical medicine and Hematology/Oncology related concepts in both the pre-clinical and clinical years, including going out to the clinical sites to work with students in rural areas to train them on how Hematology/Oncology care is delivered rurally; work with Clinical Skills and Simulation Faculty to develop cases and learning modalities through years 1-4 with Hematology/Oncology input; deliver instruction on psychiatry in each of the systems where appropriate; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on Hematology/Oncology conditions; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns. Founding Dermatology Faculty Develop curriculum and once students matriculate lead the Dermatology System course in Year 1; develop an elective course in dermatology for Year 4; teach general clinical medicine and dermatology related concepts in both the pre-clinical and clinical years, including going out to the clinical sites to work with students in rural areas to train them on how dermatology care is delivered rurally; work with Clinical Skills and Simulation Faculty to develop cases and learning modalities through years 1-4 with dermatology input; deliver instruction on dermatology in each of the systems where appropriate; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on dermatological conditions; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns. Founding Neurology Faculty Develop curriculum and once students matriculate lead the Neurology System course in Year 1, working in conjunction with neuroanatomy faculty to create a neurology/neuroanatomy course; develop an elective course in neurology for Year 4; teach general clinical medicine and neurology-related concepts in both the pre-clinical and clinical years, including going out to the clinical sites to work with students in rural areas to train them on how neurological care is delivered rurally; work with Clinical Skills and Simulation Faculty to develop cases and learning modalities through years 1-4 with neurology input; deliver instruction on neurology in each of the systems where appropriate; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on neurology conditions; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns. Founding Radiology Faculty Develop curriculum and once students matriculate serve as lead faculty in the Foundations of Biomedical Sciences course in Year 1, working in conjunction with course directors throughout Years 1 and 2 to integrate clinically-oriented radiology into each clinical system; develop an elective course in radiology for Year 4; teach general clinical medicine and radiology-related concepts in both the pre-clinical and clinical years, including going out to the clinical sites to work with students in rural areas to train them on how radiological care is delivered rurally; work with Clinical Skills and Simulation Faculty to develop cases and learning modalities through years 1-4 with radiologic input; contribute to longitudinal curriculum strands (e.g., doctor–patient relationship, communication skills, wellness); develop reflective writing assignments, and professionalism assessments; create board-style questions focused on radiology, integrated with other clinical systems; mentor students on professionalism, resilience, and career development; engage in student wellness initiatives and remediation for professionalism concerns. Additional Faculty (non-tenure track) including table trainers and lab instructors? Develop curriculum and once students matriculate , serve in non-tenure track, part-time roles, supporting hands-on training in medical education, including OMM/OPP/NMM table trainers, various lab instructors, clinical skills faculty, and clinical patient care supervision; guide students in training on osteopathic manipulative medicine (OMM) techniques, clinical skills practice, anatomy-based learning, and patient care interactions; facilitate small-group instruction; provide real-time feedback; ensure safe, effective skills development in lab and classroom settings. Duties - These roles are curriculum development focused until students matriculate in the fall of 2027, which will then transition into teaching-focus with continued curriculum development. Collaborate in development, design, and delivery of the biomedical science, clinical, and osteopathic disciplines of the entirety of the curriculum with emphasis on clinically-oriented vertical and horizontal integration across foundational and systems-based courses Contribute to the design and implementation of course and system-level curricular objectives aligned with programmatic outcomes Teach and facilitate in face-to-face classroom instruction, active learning sessions, case-based discussions, and laboratory settings, including simulation and standardized patient encounters, as appropriate to expertise Contribute to clinically relevant biomedical science content in systems courses in Years 1-2 as well as clinical rotations in Years 3-4, as appropriate Participate in curriculum delivery, assessment, and continuous quality improvement activities as part of the COM's ongoing assessment program Develop board-style questions aligned with COMLEX competencies Engage in scholarly activity, research, curricular innovation, and professional service (University, community, state, national, and international) consistent with expectations for tenure and promotion, with an emphasis on osteopathic principles and practice Advise and mentor students regarding academic progress, professional development, and career planning Participate in faculty development activities and contribute to the educational mission of the College Demonstrate professionalism, ethical conduct, and collegiality in all academic and institutional responsibilities Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University, biomedical sciences curriculum, and COM mission Position Qualifications Terminal degree (e.g., PhD, DO, MD, EdD, or PharmD) or eligible, or master’s with teaching experience for all positions, must have terminal degree (e.g., PhD, DO, MD, EdD, or PharmD) for tenure-track roles and to be considered for rank of Assistant Professor or higher. Minimum (1) year academic experience as a faculty member at an accredited US allopathic or osteopathic medical school, or other clinical, graduate, or undergraduate program with proven experience teaching clinical practice in an accredited health-sciences or nursing program. Essential Functions Strong interpersonal and team"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5483057/college-of-osteopathic-medicine-biomedical-science-faculty": {
      "title": "College of Osteopathic Medicine - Biomedical Science Faculty",
      "description": "College of Osteopathic Medicine - Biomedical Science Faculty Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02594 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 09/18/2026 Closing Date 10/19/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number 2026-06 COM Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description Position Summary & Description The IUP College of Osteopathic Medicine (IUPCOM) invites applicants for several inaugural full-time, tenure track and part-time nontenure track Biomedical Sciences faculty teaching positions beginning in the Fall of 2026. These roles offer a distinctive opportunity to contribute to the College’s development by helping to shape a forward-thinking and rurally-focused medical education program grounded in interdisciplinary collaboration, community engagement, and academic excellence with early clinical experiences. Successful candidates will demonstrate a strong and engaged commitment to medical education and play an integral role in delivering an innovative, integrated, systems-based curriculum that prioritizes active learning, clinical relevance, and interprofessional collaboration. IUP is officially classified as an R2 doctoral university institution and the College offers generous start-up financial support, research laboratory space and equipment, and other internal resources/support for scholarly pursuits. The faculty, working closely with the IUPCOM Dean's Office, will provide support for the organization, development, operationalization, and assessment of the clinically-oriented biomedical science aspects of the four-year educational curricular continuum. Biomedical Sciences Faculty Sought We are seeking multiple full-time, tenure track and part-time nontenure track faculty members at the Instructor, Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level. Note: these roles are curriculum development focused until students matriculate in the fall of 2027, which will then transition into teaching-focus with continued curriculum development. These positions include but not limited to the following disciplines/roles: Anatomy (gross anatomy and histology) Develop curriculum and once students matriculate, deliver lectures, lab instruction (cadaveric dissection, prosection, VR and imaging-based anatomy); facilitate small-group, team-based, or case-based learning sessions; direct or co-direct anatomy courses, manage lab operations, cadaver procurement, and safety; integrate clinical correlations and osteopathic principles (OMM relevance to anatomy); develop practical exams and written assessments Biochemistry & Molecular Biology Develop curriculum and once students matriculate, teach foundational biochemical pathways, molecular genetics, and metabolism in systems-based curricula; align basic science content with clinical relevance (e.g., disease mechanisms, diagnostics); collaborate with pharmacology, pathology, and clinical faculty in integrated blocks Microbiology & Immunology Develop curriculum and once students matriculate, teach infectious diseases, host-pathogen interactions, and immune system function; emphasize diagnostic reasoning, antimicrobial mechanisms, and immunologic disorders; work with infectious disease faculty on integrated teaching sessions Pathology Develop curriculum and once students matriculate, teach general and systemic pathology, often as a bridge between the foundational biomedical and clinical sciences; lead problem-based learning, case-based discussions, and clinico-pathologic correlations; create clinically oriented exam items reflecting disease mechanisms; work closely with practicing pathologists or clinicians for applied teaching Pharmacology/Pharmacogenomics Develop curriculum and once students matriculate, teach mechanisms of action, pharmacokinetics/dynamics, and therapeutics; link drug therapy to disease states in systems-based courses; collaborate with physiology and pathology faculty toward knowledge integration; develop active-learning modules (e.g., prescribing simulations, case scenarios, etc.) Physiology Develop curriculum and once students matriculate, teach normal function across organ systems (cardio, renal, respiratory, etc.); connect physiology to pathophysiology, pharmacology, and clinical medicine; lead integration experiences in small groups, case-based sessions, and simulation exercises; sequence content to support spiral/integrated curriculum models Duties – These roles are curriculum development focused until students matriculate in the fall of 2027, which will then transition into teaching-focus with continued curriculum development. Collaborate in curriculum development, design, and upon student matriculation, delivery of the biomedical sciences discipline of the entirety of the curriculum with emphasis on clinically-oriented vertical and horizontal integration across foundational and systems-based courses Contribute to the design and implementation of course and system-level curricular objectives aligned with programmatic outcomes Develop curriculum and once students matriculate, teach and facilitate in face-to-face classroom instruction, active learning sessions, case-based discussions, and laboratory settings, including anatomy and related biomedical sciences, as appropriate to expertise Contribute to clinically relevant biomedical science content in clinical clerkship syllabi in Years 3-4, as appropriate Participate in curriculum delivery, assessment, and continuous quality improvement activities as part of the COM's ongoing assessment program Develop board-style questions aligned with COMLEX competencies Engage in scholarly activity, research, curricular innovation, and professional service (University, community, state, national, and international) consistent with expectations for tenure and promotion, with an emphasis on osteopathic principles and practice Advise and mentor students regarding academic progress, professional development, and career planning Participate in faculty development activities and contribute to the educational mission of the College Demonstrate professionalism, ethical conduct, and collegiality in all academic and institutional responsibilities Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University, biomedical sciences curriculum, and COM mission Position Qualifications Terminal degree (e.g., PhD, DO, MD, EdD, or PharmD) or eligible, or master’s with teaching experience for all positions, must have terminal degree (e.g., PhD, DO, MD, EdD, or PharmD) for tenure-track roles and to be considered for rank of Assistant Professor or higher. Minimum (1) year academic experience as a faculty member at an accredited US allopathic or osteopathic medical school, or other clinical, graduate, or undergraduate program with proven experience teaching biomedical sciences in an accredited health-sciences or nursing program. Essential Functions Strong interpersonal and teamwork skills for working with interdisciplinary faculty and engaging adult learners effectively Strong foundational and expert knowledge in area of biomedical science specialization with ability to connect to clinical practice and osteopathic principles Demonstrated ability to mentor and motivate peers and learners Skills in delivering lectures, facilitating small groups (TBL/PBL), and using active learning strategies in an integrated, systems-based curriculum Ability to develop course materials, align objectives with competencies (e.g., COMLEX), and integrate content across disciplines Proficiency in writing high-quality exam questions (especially board-style questions) and assessing student performance (written exams, OSCEs, practicals) Ability to engage in research or educational scholarship, analyze data, and contribute to academic literature Skill in advising, mentoring, and supporting diverse learners, including professionalism and academic development Demonstrated leadership and productivity in the areas of medical education, clinical, or professional service Good standing with all regulatory and governmental boards and agencies IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5493920/title-ix-coordinator": {
      "title": "Title IX Coordinator",
      "description": "Title IX Coordinator Salary $66,589.00 - $86,565.00 Annually Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02598 Division President Department Office of Social Equity/Title IX Opening Date 10/14/2026 Closing Date 10/28/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number PRES 2026-3 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The Title IX Coordinator is responsible for up to date knowledge of the legal and policy standards with respect to civil rights and manages reports and processes pursuant to civil rights laws and policies, including Title IX of the Education Amendments of the 1972 Civil Rights Act; the Violence Against Women Act Reauthorization of 2012; Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964; the Americans with Disabilities Act and Sections 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; and other protected class discrimination complaints by employees and students. This role directly oversees institutional compliance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of the 1972 Civil Rights Act; the Violence Against Women Act Reauthorization of 2012; Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964; the Americans with Disabilities Act and Sections 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education System-wide and University policies prohibiting discrimination, harassment, and retaliation and all other Office of Civil Rights directives. In close coordination with IUP Public Safety, the position ensures full adherence to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and related acts, including the Violence Against Women Act Reauthorization of 2022. Collaborating across campus partnerships, the Coordinator drives educational programming and awareness campaigns regarding sexual violence, dating and domestic violence, discrimination, and other related areas. These joint initiatives also extend to providing targeted programming focused on accessibility and student success strategies. ESSENTIAL DUTIES : Maintain Regulatory Expertise: Stay current on all changing legal and policy standards regarding civil rights and institutional compliance. Manage Civil Rights Processes: Oversee reports, investigations, and formal resolution processes for complaints regarding protected-class discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. Ensure Federal & State Compliance: Monitor institutional adherence to major mandates, including Title IX, VAWA, Title VI, the ADA, Sections 503/504 of the Rehabilitation Act, and Office of Civil Rights directives. Enforce System & University Policies: Align campus practices with Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education (PASSHE) system-wide regulations and specific University anti-discrimination policies. Collaborate on Campus Safety: Partner directly with IUP Public Safety to ensure full compliance with the Jeanne Clery Act and related campus security disclosures. Deliver Prevention Programming: Work alongside campus partners to develop and implement educational campaigns addressing sexual violence, domestic/dating violence, and discrimination. Promote Campus Accessibility: Coordinate joint initiatives with campus stakeholders to provide educational resources focused on accessibility and student success strategies. WORK SCHEDULE: Monday through Friday 8:00 AM to 4:30 PM Position Qualifications MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor's degree in Higher Education Administration, Human Resources, Labor Relations, Public Administration, Legal Studies, Social Work, Psychology, Criminal Justice, or a related field. Three years of progressively responsible experience in Title IX administration, civil rights compliance, equal opportunity programs, investigations, employee relations, student conduct, higher education administration, or a related area. Experience interpreting and applying policies, regulations, and legal requirements. Experience managing sensitive and confidential matters. PREFERRED: Master's degree or Juris Doctor. Experience serving as a Title IX Coordinator or Deputy Title IX Coordinator. Experience conducting investigations involving discrimination, harassment, retaliation, or sexual misconduct. Experience with Clery Act compliance and higher education regulatory requirements. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for management employees, please click on the link below: https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/sshe-summary.pdf 01 Do you possess a bachelor's degree or higher in Higher Education Administration, Human Resources, Labor Relations, Public Administration, Legal Studies, Social Work, Psychology, Criminal Justice, or a closely related field? Yes No 02 Do you have at least three (3) years of progressively responsible experience in one or more of the following areas: Title IX administration, civil rights compliance, equal opportunity programs, investigations, employee relations, student conduct, higher education administration, or a related field? Yes No 03 Do you have experience conducting or managing investigations involving discrimination, harassment, retaliation, sexual misconduct, employee relations, student conduct, or other civil rights-related matters, and/or experience with Title IX, Clery Act compliance, or related regulatory requirements? Yes No 04 Do you have experience serving as a Title IX Coordinator, Deputy Title IX Coordinator, or in a role with primary responsibility for Title IX compliance? Yes No 05 Do you possess a Master's degree or Juris Doctor (JD)? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5495244/associate-director-for-academic-career-and-professional-development-sua3": {
      "title": "Associate Director for Academic, Career, and Professional Development (SUA3)",
      "description": "Associate Director for Academic, Career, and Professional Development (SUA3) Salary $61,966.00 Annually Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02599 Division Academic Affairs Department Career and Professional Development Center Opening Date 10/05/2026 Closing Date 10/20/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number AA 2026-30 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description This position is posted in accordance with the (SCUPA) Collective Bargaining Unit. POSITION SUMMARY: Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applicants for an Associate Director for Academic, Career, and Professional Development (SUA3) in the Career and Professional Development Center Department. The team member in this role performs professional administrative work in conjunction with the director and other team members of the Career and Professional Development Center with a focus on student success, academic readiness, career readiness, and professional development in alignment with the university's strategic initiatives. The position supports student persistence, retention, academic achievement, career exploration, experiential learning, and successful transition to employment or graduate study through individualized coaching, developmental programming, and campus partnerships. ESSENTIAL DUTIES: Oversee and manage the training, supervision, professional development, and evaluation of graduate team members. Prepare reports as requested and required. Prepare, update, and edit departmental publications and marketing materials; including the departmental programming calendar. Maintain weekly contact hours for individual academic and career readiness coaching and education appointments to meet the needs of students, alumni, and other constituents. Identify, plan, organize, facilitate, collaborate, and present academic and career readiness programs and workshops to various audiences. Collaborate with director and team to determine appropriate technological solutions utilized for academic and career readiness programming (oversee and implement technological solutions when needed). Serve as the campus liaison for The Washington Center (TWC) and The Disney College Program (DCP); including coordination with IUP faculty and TWC and DCP representatives for recruiting, registration, and billing/funding procedures. Partner with department internship supervisors to coordinate internship opportunities for students. Develop communication plans to publicize planned activities and regular communication to students, faculty, and staff regarding department programs, events, and initiatives. Seek and establish programming sponsorships, partnerships, and collaborations with internal and external constituents. Assist with cultivating long-term relationships with employers. Manage the implementation of employer recruiting activities for entry-level employment and internships, including information sessions, interviews, and other marketing strategies directed to students. Educate students on negotiation of offers, overall ethical and professional conduct, resume and cover letter writing, informational interviewing, interview preparation, time management and prioritization, and interview cancellations. Serve as a department representative for a variety of events, including recruiting visits to employer sites; participation in national, state, and regional professional associations, conferences, and career fair organizations; hosting organizations on campus for employer development and cultivation purposes; and Orientation, Admissions events and other such programming. Actively engage with professional organizations, including assuming leadership roles within those organizations and engage in professional development and benchmarking opportunities. WORK SCHEDULE: Monday through Friday 8:00 AM to 4:30 PM Position Qualifications MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: Master's degree in higher education (or related field) with 2-3 years of experience and specialization in career services, success coaching, orientation or related work. PREFERRED: 3-5 years of experience and specialization in career services, success coaching, and/or orientation. Candidates must have the communication skills and cross-cultural abilities to maximize their effectiveness with diverse groups of students, colleagues, and community members. Candidates must communicate effectively and perform well in the interview(s). IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for SCUPA employees, please click on the link below: http://www.passhe.edu/inside/HR/syshr/benefit_highlights/PEBTF_Highlights.pdf 01 Do you have a master's degree in higher education (or related field) with 2-3 years of experience and specialization in career services, success coaching, orientation or related work? Yes No 02 Do you have 3-5 years of experience and specialization in career services, success coaching, and/or orientation? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5509875/executive-director-of-academic-and-career-readiness-mgr-200": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Academic and Career Readiness - MGR 200",
      "description": "Executive Director of Academic and Career Readiness - MGR 200 Salary $88,999.00 - $115,698.00 Annually Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02606 Division Academic Affairs Department Career and Professional Development Center Opening Date 10/19/2026 Closing Date 10/29/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number AA 2026-32 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description POSITION SUMMARY: The Executive Director of Academic and Career Readiness provides leadership and strategic oversight for programs and services that support students throughout the academic life cycle, from pre-enrollment and onboarding through persistence, graduation, and career placement. The position is responsible for managing staff, resources, assessment initiatives, and collaborative partnerships that advance student engagement, retention, persistence, and post-graduation outcomes. ESSENTIAL DUTIES: Establishes strategic goals, priorities, and performance measures for academic and career readiness programs, ensuring alignment with institutional objectives related to student success, retention, career outcomes, and workforce preparation. Provides leadership and supervision for professional and student staff, including hiring, onboarding, training, performance management, workload coordination, and fostering a collaborative and student-centered culture. Serve on university committees as requested and appropriate. Serve in leadership roles within professional organizations to benefit IUP and its students. Develops and maintains collaborative partnerships with academic departments, employers, community organizations, and campus stakeholders to align academic and career readiness services, expand experiential learning opportunities, and strengthen workforce readiness initiatives. Oversees personnel who plan and implement academic and career readiness events, including orientation programs, career fairs, employer engagement activities, workshops, and leadership development opportunities. Collaborates with campus departments, employers, alumni, and community partners to develop, promote, and implement events that support student transition, academic achievement, career exploration, workforce preparation, and experiential learning. Oversees assessment and continuous improvement efforts by analyzing program outcomes, student engagement data, and service effectiveness metrics to inform decision-making, enhance program quality, and support accreditation and reporting requirements. WORK SCHEDULE: Monday through Friday 8:00 AM to 4:30 PM Position Qualifications MINIMUM: Master's Degree in appropriate academic discipline (e.g., Counseling, Higher Education, or related field) 3-5 years experience in career services, student success, and/or new student transition PREFERRED: 7-8 years experience in career services, student success, and/or new student transition IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for management employees, please click on the link below: https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/sshe-summary.pdf 01 Do you have a master's degree in counseling, higher education, or a related field? Yes No 02 Do you have 3-5 years' experience in career services, student success, and/or new student transition? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5510211/clerical-assistant-2-eberly-college-of-business": {
      "title": "Clerical Assistant 2 - Eberly College of Business",
      "description": "Clerical Assistant 2 - Eberly College of Business Salary $36,831.00 Annually Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02607 Division Academic Affairs Department Eberly College of Business Opening Date 10/12/2026 Closing Date 10/22/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number AA 2026-31 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description THIS POSITION IS POSTED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE AFSCME COLLECTIVE BARGAINING UNIT SUMMARY: The position provides clerical and office support for the School of International Management (SIM) and Special Programs within the Eberly College of Business (ECOB). The individual will ensure that the academic and administrative functions of the college are conducted efficiently and effectively. The primary focus of this position is to support the SIM and special programs, which involves serving the needs of all its constituents including students, faculty, alumni/friends, international and local partners. Review the PA Specifications for this Job Title. The above duties are normal for this position. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the classification if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment for this classification. Other duties may be required and assigned. ESSENTIAL DUTIES: Establishing and following communication plans with existing international partners pertaining to student admissions, academic standing (probation/dismissal) and program operations. There are cultural and technical differences in each of these countries and regions, in addition to time differences. Supporting the coordination of faculty schedules and travel dates to offshore locations and providing logistical support based on teaching schedules while balancing cost and convenience of travel. Processing travel reimbursement after approval. Processing of faculty contract paperwork through the Provost’s Office and coordinating the mandatory international travel paperwork for all Eberly travelers. Supporting nurturing of corporate partnerships that can result in company visits, guest speakers, internships, and placements. Processing internships for international students, including liaising with employers and the IUP OIE to ensure compliance with institutional policies and federal regulations. Supporting in alumni engagement initiatives, including organizing events, maintaining alumni database and facilitating communications between alumni and current students. Working with procurement on purchases. Working with graduate coordinators in allocating Graduate Assistantships. Providing clerical support for annual SIM and Eberly events and programs including but not limited to Discover India, India Day, Graduation dinner, Biz Wiz High School Quiz Competition, Eberly Golf Classic, Business Day, Summer Certificate Program, etc. Maintaining relevant websites. Assisting faculty and administration in Eberly outreach activities pertaining to high schools and community colleges. Providing clerical support to the off-campus graduate programs including the PhD program in Pittsburgh East. WORK SCHEDULE: Monday through Friday 7:30 AM to 4:00 PM Position Qualifications MINIMUM EXPERIENCE AND TRAINING: Six months as a Clerical Assistant 1 (commonwealth title); or Graduation from high school OR An equivalent combination of experience and training. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for AFSCME employees, please click on the link below: pebtf-summary.pdf (passhe.edu) 01 Do you have six months as a Clerical Assistant 1 (commonwealth title) or graduated from high school or an equivalent combination of experience and training? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5512055/senior-systems-analyst-onesis-cadm": {
      "title": "Senior Systems Analyst - OneSIS CADM",
      "description": "Senior Systems Analyst - OneSIS CADM Salary $76,539.00 - $99,500.00 Annually Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Temporary Job Number 02608 Division Academic Affairs Department IT Services - OneSIS Opening Date 10/12/2026 Closing Date 10/22/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number AA 2026-7 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description SUMMARY: Reporting to an IT Services Coordinator, this position is the most senior purely technical role within IT Services. The incumbent is responsible for implementing assigned projects and performing senior-level administration of databases, networks, and systems, as assigned. This position manages daily operational issues for production systems and participates in the evaluation, selection, design, and implementation of new systems and networks. This role evaluates institutional practices and re-engineers processes to improve operations and services. The incumbent is responsible for all phases of the software life cycle, including analysis, design, development, implementation, and documentation, and works collaboratively with fellow IT Services employees to implement new technologies. In addition, this position provides leadership, subject matter expertise, research, documentation, and consulting services to support the work of committees, teams, and individuals, as assigned. This is a temporary, grant-funded position ending June 30, 2029, with the possibility of extension contingent upon funding renewal. ESSENTIAL DUTIES: Performs senior level administration of databases, networks and systems, as assigned. Manages daily operational issues for production systems. Provides leadership, subject matter expertise, performs research, provides documentation and consulting to support the work of committees, teams and individuals, as assigned. Responsible for implementing projects as assigned. Works with fellow IT Services employees to implement new technologies. Evaluates institutional practices and re-engineers processes to improve operations and services. Participates in the evaluation, selection, design, and implementation of new systems and networks. WORK SCHEDULE: Monday through Friday 8:00 AM to 4:30 PM WORK LOCATION: This position is 100% remote. Position Qualifications MINIMUM: B.S. Computer Science, Management Information Systems, related field or equivalent experience. Minimum seven years of experience in a variety of information technology roles, with demonstrated increases in levels of responsibility. Minimum of five years either application development, database administration, systems administration, or network administration. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for management employees, please click on the link below: https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/sshe-summary.pdf 01 Do you have a Bachelor of Science degree in Computer Science, Management Information Systems, a related field or equivalent experience? Yes No 02 Do you have a minimum of seven years of experience in a variety of information technology roles, with demonstrated increases in levels of responsibility? Yes No 03 Do you have a minimum of five years of either application development, database administration, systems administration, or network administration? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5514087/labrynth-director": {
      "title": "Labrynth Director",
      "description": "Labrynth Director Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 02611 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 10/15/2026 Closing Date 11/15/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number ASDSPTemp2027 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The IUP Labyrinth Center is a sponsored program that supports students with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD) and other related disabilities. Students enroll in a one-credit course each semester, and receive academic and life coaching, supervised study sessions, and peer and faculty mentoring. Students can also participate in extra-curricular activities outside of the Labyrinth Center for additional enrichment and entertainment. The department seeks candidates whose teaching, research, and/or service has prepared them to contribute to IUP’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in higher education. Position Qualifications Minimum Qualifications · Master’s degree in Special Education, Counseling, Higher Education, Psychology, Social Work, Rehabilitation Services, Student Affairs, or a related field. · Minimum of three years of professional experience working with individuals with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD) and/or related disabilities. · Experience providing academic support, coaching, counseling, or student services in an educational setting. · Demonstrated supervisory, organizational, and administrative skills. · Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. · Ability to collaborate effectively with students, families, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications · Experience in higher education disability services or college transition programs. · Experience developing and teaching curriculum or student success courses. · Knowledge of evidence-based practices supporting neurodiverse college students. · Experience with program assessment, data analysis, and reporting. · Familiarity with mentoring and peer-support programs. · Grant development experience. Essential Functions · Knowledge of Autism Spectrum Disorder and related disabilities within a postsecondary context. · Understanding of student development theory and inclusive educational practices. · Ability to develop supportive relationships while maintaining appropriate professional boundaries. · Ability to manage multiple priorities and complex student needs. · Strong problem-solving and conflict-resolution skills. · Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and student success. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/2829734/non-credit-instructor-american-language-institute": {
      "title": "Non-Credit Instructor - American Language Institute",
      "description": "Non-Credit Instructor - American Language Institute Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Temporary Job Number 01502 Division Academic Affairs Department American Language Institute - NCL Opening Date 01/18/2024 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The Office of International Education in the Division of Academic Affairs at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applications for American Language Institute Instructors. The ALI intensive English program supports students in developing English language skills and a deeper understanding of U.S. academic culture. The position reports to the Executive Director of the American Language Institute. ALI instructors are responsible for designing course syllabi, selecting texts and material for classes, planning lessons, keeping attendance records, assessing students’ progress, and maintaining a positive learning environment. Instructors accommodate students’ learning needs and help them prepare for a successful transition to higher education in the United States. Noninstructional responsibilities include assisting with new student orientation, administering program assessments, participating in staff meetings, engaging in professional development, and submitting required records including grade and attendance reports and syllabi. The instructor will be required to perform the tasks as required/requested in support of the American Language Institute and the university. Position Qualifications Required: Relevant teaching experience and master’s degree in TESOL, applied linguistics, or closely related field. Experience successfully working with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Proficiency with instructional technology. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Competencies: To perform the job successfully, an individual should demonstrate the following competencies. Adaptability/Flexibility – embraces change with innovation, courage, and resiliency. Promote Key Values – consistently demonstrates Indiana University of Pennsylvania’s values. Communicates Effectively – shares information and engages in candid and open dialogue. Focuses on Customers – works to exceed expectations of internal and external customers. Produces Results – directs action toward achieving goals that are critical to Indiana University of Pennsylvania’s success. Manage Own Performance – plans and organizes time and priorities to achieve expected results. Uses Sound Business Judgement – uses knowledge of the field and common sense to make the best decisions. Teamwork/Collaboration -excels at building partnerships and working as part of a team. Preferred: University-based intensive English teaching and international teaching experience. Professional involvement in the field, including membership of professional organizations, presentations, and publications. Essential Functions The work of this position occurs in a typical office environment. Although infrequent, periods of heavy exertion may occur. Incumbent must have the following abilities: Ability to travel to meeting/training sites. Communicate both orally and in writing to issue, receive and carry out instructions and orders effectively and to convey information to a variety of co-workers and the general public. Use a variety of common office machines such as telephones, calculators, copiers, computer terminals, keyboards, video display terminals, auxiliary printers, and similar equipment. Operate office equipment which may require stooping, kneeling, bending, stretching and prolonged standing. Provide assistance and guidance to internal and external customers. Follow oral and written instructions. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply for this position, please submit a letter of application, a current curriculum vitae, and unofficial copies of transcripts via our online application system: https: //www.schooljobs . com/careers/iupedu . If the degree listed as required for this position was earned at IUP-no official transcripts are required to be submitted as part of this employment application. IUP will verify IUP obtained degrees and only request official transcripts from candidates if needed. Committed to excellence through diversity, IUP is an equal opportunity employer M/F/D/V and is a proud member of the State System of Higher Education. All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. Agency: Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address : 1011 South Drive Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone : 724-357-2431 Website : http://www.iup.edu/employment IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. Non-mgmt, non-represented employees Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/4300834/criminal-justice-training-center-non-credit-instructor": {
      "title": "Criminal Justice Training Center - Non-Credit Instructor",
      "description": "Criminal Justice Training Center - Non-Credit Instructor Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 02097 Division Academic Affairs Department Criminal Justice Training Center Opening Date 12/04/2023 Closing Date Continuous Reference Number 9999 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description Summary The Criminal Justice Training Center in the College of Health and Human Services at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applicants for various non-credit instructional positions. Available Roles: 1. Physical Conditioning Instructor 2. First Aid and CPR Instructor 3. Application of Force Special Instructor 4. Firearms Special Instructor 5. Patrol Vehicle Operation Special Instructor 6. General Instruction IUP Instructors - PT Position (Adjunct) - Must be eligible for MPOETC instructor certification to apply. $30 per hour. CNX Instructors - PT Position (Adjunct) Position Qualifications Physical Conditioning Instructor Minimum Education and Training Physical Conditioning - Provide documentation of successful completion of an Instructor Development course and training or education which evidences expertise as a physical conditioning instructor. Must be certified by MPOETC as a Physical Conditioning instructor and receive an instructor identification number. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Approved Physical Conditioning certification, five years police experience (must document), a Bachelor of Arts Degree (transcript required), and Instructor Development Course (copy of certificate required). First Aid and CPR Instructor Minimum Education and Training Must possess a current Instructor Certification issued by the American Red Cross, the American Heart Association, the Department of Health or other agency approved by the Department of Health. (40 hour curriculum). Must be certified by MPOETC as a First Aid and CPR instructor and receive an instructor identification number. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Approved First Aid and CPR certification, five years police experience (must document), a Bachelor of Arts Degree (transcript required), and Instructor Development Course (copy of certificate required). Application of Force Special Instructor Minimum Experience & Training Provide documentation of successful completion of an Instructor Development course and training or education which evidences expertise as a defensive tactics instructor. Must be certified by MPOETC as a Defensive Tactics instructor and receive an instructor identification number. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Approved Defensive Tactics Instructor, five years police experience (must document), a Bachelor of Arts Degree (transcript required), and Instructor Development Course (copy of certificate required). Firearms Special Instructor Minimum Experience & Training Possess a current Police Firearms Instructor rating from the National Rifle Association, the State Police, the Federal Bureau of Investigation, Smith and Wesson Academy, the Philadelphia Police Academy, United States Secret Service, or other certification approved by the Commission. Must be certified by MPOETC as a Firearms instructor and receive an instructor identification number. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Approved Firearms certification, five years police experience (must document), a Bachelor of Arts Degree (transcript required), and Instructor Development Course (copy of certificate required). Patrol Vehicle Operation Special Instructor Minimum Experience & Training Provide documentation of successful completion of an Instructor Development course and an instructor's course in emergency vehicle operation or police driver proficiency. Must be certified by MPOETC as a Patrol Vehicle Operator instructor and receive an instructor identification number. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Approved Patrol Vehicle Operator, five years police experience (must document), a Bachelor of Arts Degree (transcript required), and Instructor Development Course (copy of certificate required). General Instruction Minimum Experience & Training Three years police experience (must document), a Bachelor of Arts Degree (transcript required), and either an acceptable Instructor Development Course (copy of certificate required) or a teaching certificate issued by the Department of Education (copy of certificate required) or have full-time employment with academic rank at an accredited college or university (must document). OR Four years police experience (must document), an Associate of Arts Degree (transcript required), and either an acceptable Instructor Development Course (copy of certificate required), or a teaching certificate issued by the Department of Education (copy of certificate required) or have full-time employment with academic rank at an accredited college or university (must document). OR Five years police experience (must document), and either an acceptable Instructor Development Course (copy of certificate required), or a teaching certificate issued by the Department of Education (copy of certificate required) or have full-time employment with academic rank at an accredited college or university (must document). OR Attorney licensed to practice in Pennsylvania (include copy of current bar card). Must be certified by MPOETC as a general instructor and receive an instructor identification number. Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Five years police experience (must document), a Bachelor of Arts Degree (transcript required), and Instructor Development Course (copy of certificate required). Essential Functions The work of this position occurs in a typical office environment. Although infrequent, periods of heavy exertion may occur. Incumbent must have the following abilities: Ability to travel to field locations and meeting/training sites by motor vehicle when required. Communicate both orally and in writing to issue, receive and carry out instructions and orders effectively and to convey information to a variety of co-workers and the general public. U se a variety of common office machines such as telephones, calculators, copiers, computer terminals, keyboards, video display terminals, auxiliary printers and similar equipment. Employee must be able to observe and react to hazard warnings, backup alarms, flashing lights, voice commands and hand signals. Perform manual duties such as lifting and carrying various weight limits. Operate office equipment which may require stooping, kneeling, bending, stretching and prolonged standing. Provide assistance and guidance to internal and external customers. Follow oral and written instructions. Special Instructions to Applicants All applicants must submit a cover letter and resume as an attachment via this online application system at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Application review will continue until all positions are filled. You will receive a confirmation email when your application has been successfully submitted. Please do not fax, mail or e-mail any documentation. Committed to excellence through diversity, IUP is an equal opportunity employer M/F/D/V and is a proud member of the State System of Higher Education. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon confirmation of work eligibility and satisfactory completion of all pre-employment background checks. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. Non-mgmt, non-represented employees Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5071141/department-of-nursing-temporary-faculty": {
      "title": "Department of Nursing - Temporary Faculty",
      "description": "Department of Nursing - Temporary Faculty Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time &/or Part Time / Temporary Job Number 02387 Division Academic Affairs Department Nursing Opening Date 09/05/2025 Closing Date Continuous Reference Number 9999 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The Department of Nursing at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applicants for several temporary faculty positions for the 2025-2026 academic year, including summer 2026. IUP offers CCNE accredited programs leading to a Bachelor of Science in Nursing and Master of Science in Nursing (education and administration tracks). IUP also offers a PhD in Nursing with an emphasis in nursing education. Duties Candidates must demonstrate current clinical expertise and will be required to teach a variety of undergraduate courses throughout the curriculum. Faculty may have the opportunity to teach in the masters and PhD nursing programs. The successful candidate may be assigned to work at off campus sites and/or provide instruction through distance education. Position Qualifications Required: Master of Science in Nursing is preferred. Candidates without a graduate degree may be considered when fully qualified faculty are not available and shall teach under guidance of another qualified faculty member in the department. Candidates without a graduate degree in nursing shall have a baccalaureate degree in nursing and evidence of a plan for obtaining a graduate degree in nursing within a 5-year period. Candidates without a degree in nursing but hold a graduate degree in a subject area pertinent to their area of teaching may be considered to teach in a specialized area of health care practice. Candidates must also possess a current USA RN license. All candidates must communicate effectively and perform well during interview(s), including a teaching demonstration. The department seeks candidates whose research, teaching, or service has prepared them to contribute to our commitment to diversity and inclusion in higher education. Essential Functions To perform the essential functions of the job, this position requires working at third-party sites that are not owned or controlled by the University. These sites may have various health and safety requirements for IUP employees to enter their facilities. These requirements may include, but are not limited to, providing proof or certification that you are fully vaccinated against the SARS-CoV-2 virus and its variants, influenza, and possibly other transmissible viruses. The selected candidate for this position will have to adhere to all other policies of the field sites, which may include, but not be limited to, background clearance checks, drug testing, and medical clearance. Academic faculty must have, and maintain the physical and mental abilities, communicative skills, and stamina necessary to carry out the essential functions of their positions in teaching, research, scholarship, and service. Work involves sitting most of the time, but may involve standing to a significant degree, walking for brief periods of time and may include driving requirements. Faculty must be able to: Teach courses assigned by the departmental chair on a schedule made of a combination of standard class-meeting times as determined to meet instructional needs and adhere to the requirements of the department's curriculum. Teach courses for a mandated number of contact hours per week over a full semester and meet university expectations for final exams. Present course material in a clear and organized manner using methodologies appropriate to the discipline. Evaluate student work fairly and promptly. Perform the physical requirements of laboratory, field work, studio work, or other activities outside typical classroom instruction if applicable. Maintain current knowledge of the discipline through continued scholarly activity and research. Participate actively in assignments necessary to advance the service and/or outreach of the department, college, and university. Service and scholarship responsibilities are commensurate with assigned workload. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply for this position: P lease submit a letter of application, a current curriculum vitae, unofficial copies of transcripts, and the names and email addresses of three references via our online application system: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu . Automated reference requests and a confirmation email will be generated upon submission of your application. Candidates who fail to submit all of the aforementioned materials will not be considered. If the degree listed as required for this position was earned at IUP - no official transcripts are required to be submitted as part of this employment application. IUP HR will verify IUP obtained degrees and only request official transcripts from candidates if needed. Official transcripts will be required prior to hire date for applicants who did not earn the required degrees at IUP. Committed to excellence through diversity, IUP is an equal opportunity employer M/F/D/V and is a proud member of the State System of Higher Education. All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5071195/department-of-allied-and-public-health-respiratory-care-temporary-faculty": {
      "title": "Department of Allied and Public Health - Respiratory Care - Temporary Faculty",
      "description": "Department of Allied and Public Health - Respiratory Care - Temporary Faculty Location IUP at Pittsburgh East Job Type Full Time &/or Part Time / Temporary Job Number 02388 Division Academic Affairs Department Allied and Public Health Opening Date 09/08/2025 Closing Date Continuous Reference Number 9999 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The Respiratory Care Program at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applications for anticipated part-time, and full-time temporary positions at the Instructor and Assistant Professor level for the academic year 2025-2026. IUP offers a CoARC accredited program leading to a Bachelor of Science in Respiratory Care, within the department of Allied and Public Health. The successful candidate(s) will be assigned to the Pittsburgh East regional campus, and may be assigned to work at off campus sites and/or provide instruction through distance education. Duties The successful candidate(s) will be expected to teach a variety of undergraduate courses throughout the curriculum (including instruction in the didactic, laboratory, and clinical setting). Engage in scholarly work in the field and participate in related university and community services. Position Qualifications Required: Bachelor's degree in respiratory care. Hold a valid Registered Respiratory Therapy (RRT) credential and current state license. Preferred: Master's degree in Respiratory Care. An established record of accomplishment in teaching, scholarship, and service. The department seeks candidates whose teaching, research, and/or service has prepared them to contribute to IUP’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in higher education. Essential Functions To perform the essential functions of the job, this position requires working at third-party sites that are not owned or controlled by the University These sites may have various health and safety requirements for IUP employees to enter their facilities. These requirements may include, but are not limited to, providing proof or certification that you are fully vaccinated against the SARS-CoV-2 virus and its variants, influenza, and possibly other transmissible viruses. The selected candidate for this position will have to adhere to all other policies of the field sites, which may include, but not be limited to, background clearance checks, drug testing, and medical clearance. Academic faculty must have, and maintain the physical and mental abilities, communicative skills, and stamina necessary to carry out the essential functions of their positions in teaching, research, scholarship, and service. Work involves sitting most of the time, but may involve standing to a significant degree, walking for brief periods of time and may include driving requirements. Faculty must be able to: Teach courses assigned by the departmental chair on a schedule made of a combination of standard class-meeting times as determined to meet instructional needs and adhere to the requirements of the department's curriculum. Teach courses for a mandated number of contact hours per week over a full semester and meet university expectations for final exams. Present course material in a clear and organized manner using methodologies appropriate to the discipline. Evaluate student work fairly and promptly. Perform the physical requirements of laboratory, field work, studio work, or other activities outside typical classroom instruction if applicable. Maintain current knowledge of the discipline through continued scholarly activity and research. Participate actively in assignments necessary to advance the service and/or outreach of the department, college, and university. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply for this position: P lease submit a letter of application, a current curriculum vitae, unofficial copies of transcripts, and the names and email addresses of three references via our online application system: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu . Automated reference requests and a confirmation email will be generated upon submission of your application. Candidates who fail to submit all of the aforementioned materials will not be considered. If the degree listed as required for this position was earned at IUP - no official transcripts are required to be submitted as part of this employment application. IUP HR will verify IUP obtained degrees and only request official transcripts from candidates if needed. Official transcripts will be required prior to hire date for applicants who did not earn the required degrees at IUP. Committed to excellence through diversity, IUP is an equal opportunity employer M/F/D/V and is a proud member of the State System of Higher Education. All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5120769/department-of-allied-and-public-health-temporary-part-time-faculty": {
      "title": "Department of Allied and Public Health - Temporary Part-Time Faculty",
      "description": "Department of Allied and Public Health - Temporary Part-Time Faculty Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 02405 Division Academic Affairs Department Allied and Public Health Opening Date 10/23/2025 Reference Number 9999 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The Department of Allied and Public Health at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applications for part-time, temporary, non-tenure track Professor positions. These positions involve developing curriculum for the proposed College of Osteopathic Medicine (COM). The proposed COM is currently progressing through accreditation phases and has reached the point of developing curriculum. These positions will work closely with the Dean’s Office in the proposed COM, the APH faculty, and other associated departments at IUP. The positions will be responsible for creating the curriculum and course objectives following the course sequencing outlined for the proposed COM with a focus on the clinical aspects related to (1) primary care practice, (2) osteopathic manipulative medicine (OMM), or (3) specialty medicine. The proposed curriculum sequencing will be used to create the course descriptions and course learning objectives. Duties The successful candidate for each position will be expected to develop curriculum topics following the course sequencing outlined for the proposed COM in areas of 1) primary care practice, (2) osteopathic manipulative medicine, or (3) specialty medicine coursework with an emphasis on integrating core content focused on the respective position into clinically focused courses. Develop learning objectives for the proposed COM curriculum in the areas of 1) primary care practice, (2) osteopathic manipulative medicine, or (3) specialty medicine coursework with an emphasis on integrating core content focused on the respective position into clinically focused courses by linking course and programmatic objectives. Assist with development of syllabi, coursework learning objectives and curricula for clinical rotations by integrating OMM/OPP into each of the clinical disciplines. Design a progressive format of medical science presentation, consistent with the proposed curriculum sequencing. Design appropriate laboratory experiences for medical students in an integrated curriculum. Collaborate with current IUP faculty. Work collaboratively with other temporary faculty of the proposed COM and the COM Deans to ensure that curriculum development is not duplicated and is pedagogically sound through vertical and horizontal integration. Position Qualifications Required General Qualifications: Terminal degree (DO or MD); DO preferred Board Certification in the respective clinical specialty. Current active and unrestricted medical licensure with record free of past disciplinary actions against the medical license. Three (3) years academic experience as (1) a faculty member at an accredited United States DO or MD medical school or (2) a faculty member in a ACGME-Accredited Graduate Medical Education program. Demonstrated experience in the development of medical curricula and coursework in osteopathic or allopathic medical schools. Documented scholarship in the respective clinical area and/or medical education Ability to work effectively in an inter-disciplinary environment Required Primary Care Position Specific Qualifications: Maintenance of AOA or ABMS board certification in primary care discipline(s) (family medicine, pediatrics, or internal medicine) required. Proven experience in teaching and academic leadership in a medical education setting through teaching of in primary care discipline(s) (family medicine, pediatrics, or internal medicine) required. Required Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine (OMM) Position Specific Qualifications: DO (from a COCA-accredited medical school) Maintenance of AOA board certification by the AOBNMM or a Certificate of Specialty Proficiency in OMM (C-SPOMM) required. Proven experience in teaching and academic leadership in a medical education setting through teaching of in OMM/OPP in medical education setting. Actively seeing patients and/or actively practicing OPP/NMM preferred Required Specialty Medicine Position Specific Requirements: Maintenance of AOA or ABMS board certification in a specialty care discipline (e.g., internal medicine subspecialty fellowship; OB/GYN, Psychiatry; Emergency Medicine; Surgery; etc.). Proven experience in teaching and academic leadership in a medical education setting through teaching in specialty medicine discipline in medical education setting. Actively seeing patients and/or actively practicing specialty medicine discipline preferred Preferred: Additional coursework or degrees with a focus on medical education leadership and/or curriculum pedagogy A substantial record of success as an educator with experience in teaching foundational concepts which are relevant to medical education. Preferred candidates shall have teaching experience in an academic setting and health delivery. Experience with curricular and instructional design and training or experience in educational theory and/or evaluation preferred. Essential Functions Academic faculty must have, and maintain the physical and mental abilities, communicative skills, and stamina necessary to carry out essential functions of their position. Faculty must be able to: Have and maintain good standing with all regulatory and governmental boards and agencies. Demonstrate leadership and administrative experience in clinical, professional, or educational settings. Values collaboration, mutual support and team cohesion with colleagues. Present knowledge of instructional technologies is desirable. Present strong organization, interpersonal, and planning skills. Present strong verbal and written communication skills and excellent presentation skills. Demonstrate the ability to work in a team and flexibility to work with others in a variety of circumstances. Demonstrate the ability to problem-solve by analyzing issues and creating action plans. Demonstrate the ability to work with different computer programs and databases and software. Demonstrate the ability to present the COM in an appropriate and positive fashion in public meetings, testimony and public appearances. Maintain professional literacy in academic field. Possess excellent oral and written communication skills. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply for this position: Please submit a letter of application, and a current curriculum vitae via our online application system: https:www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu. At a later date, we will request that you submit unofficial copies of transcripts, and the names and email addresses for three references. Committed to excellence through diversity, IUP is an equal opportunity employer M/F/D/V and is a proud member of the State System of Higher Education. All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5234185/college-of-osteopathic-medicine-founding-chair-omm-opp-tenure-track-faculty": {
      "title": "College of Osteopathic Medicine - Founding Chair OMM/OPP - Tenure Track Faculty",
      "description": "College of Osteopathic Medicine - Founding Chair OMM/OPP - Tenure Track Faculty Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02455 Division Academic Affairs Department Allied and Public Health Opening Date 02/18/2026 Reference Number OMOPMED Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The College of Osteopathic Medicine (COM) at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applications for an open rank, Founding Chairperson, tenure track faculty positions: Chair of Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine and Osteopathic Principles and Practices (OMM/OPP); This position will report and work closely with the Dean’s Office in the College of Osteopathic Medicine at IUP. The position will be responsible for providing support for the development, operationalization, delivery, and assessment of the discipline specific area of medicine focused clinical education curriculum. Essential Duties: Develop curriculum and course/system curricular objectives for coursework in the COM, with an emphasis on integrating core OMM/OPP, specialty medicine, or primary care- related content into clinically oriented courses, including linking course and programmatic objectives. Develop the curriculum for the OMM/OPP, specialty medicine, or primary care- longitudinal coursework throughout all 4-years of the COM curriculum. Coordinate the integration of OMM/OPP, specialty medicine, or primary care- related content into clinical system courses in Years 1-2 and clinical clerkship syllabi in Years 3-4. Develop, deliver, integrate, implement, and teach COM pre-clinical OMM/OPP, specialty medicine, or primary care - curriculum and student assessment measures, including assisting the other clinical Chairs with the standardized patient and simulated patient encounter programs housed within the Clinical Skills curriculum. Actively teach in face-to-face classroom and clinical skills training settings for in-person development and delivery of curriculum. Participate in research and scholarly activity with emphasis on osteopathic medicine principles and practice. Actively participate in student career advising and mentoring. Work collaboratively with the faculty Chairs of the other COM disciplines (Primary Care, Specialty Medicine, and Biomedical Sciences) and the COM Associate Deans to ensure that curriculum development is not duplicative and is pedagogically sound with both planned vertical and horizontal integration relative to OMM/OPP, specialty medicine, or primary care. Assist in the development of syllabi, coursework, learning objectives, and curricula for clinical clerkships, integrating OMM/OPP, specialty medicine, or primary care into each of the clinical disciplines. Support in planning and delivering ongoing faculty development activities based on curricular interests and expertise. Participate in curriculum development, delivery, assessment, and quality improvement as a part of the proposed COM’s ongoing quality improvement and assessment program. Demonstrate the highest standards of professionalism and ethical behavior in all aspects of personal and professional actions and performance. Demonstrate and role model an ongoing ability to work cooperatively with colleagues, supervisors, and support staff. Other duties as assigned related to curriculum development, related to OMM/OPP, specialty medicine, or primary care, for the 4-year osteopathic medical education program. Note: Discipline chair duties are performed for the duration of the incumbent serving in that position in accordance with the CBA/Side Letter, with term up for re-election in 2029. Position Qualifications Required: Education, Experience and Certification Terminal degree (DO or MD); DO degree preferred Three (3) years academic experience as a faculty member at an accredited US osteopathic medical school with proven experience in developing curricula for OMM/OPP/NMM, specialty medicine, or primary care- Current active and unrestricted medical licensure and board certification (as below); record free of past disciplinary actions against the medical license Maintenance of AOA board certification by the AOBNMM or a Certificate of Special Proficiency in OMM (C-SPOMM), specialty of medicine, or primary care required with proven experience in teaching and academic leadership in a medical education setting. Demonstrated excellence as faculty with experience in development of medical curricula and coursework in osteopathic medical schools or in GME programming Additional coursework or degrees with a focus on medical education leadership and/or curriculum pedagogy (preferred) Active seeing patients and in actively medical practice (preferred) Skills & Experience Demonstrate academic leadership, effective communication, and time management skills Team player Demonstrate ability to mentor and motivate peers Demonstrated leadership and productivity in the areas of clinical or professional service and education Good standing with all regulatory and governmental boards and agencies Demonstrated leadership and administrative experience in clinical, professional or educational settings, preferred Essential Functions Academic faculty must have, and maintain the physical and mental abilities, communicative skills, and stamina necessary to carry out essential functions of their position. Faculty must be able to: Have and maintain good standing with all regulatory and governmental boards and agencies. Demonstrate leadership and administrative experience in clinical, professional, or educational settings. Values collaboration, mutual support and team cohesion with colleagues. Present knowledge of instructional technologies is desirable. Present strong organization, interpersonal, and planning skills. Present strong verbal and written communication skills and excellent presentation skills. Demonstrate the ability to work in a team and flexibility to work with others in a variety of circumstances. Demonstrate the ability to problem-solve by analyzing issues and creating action plans. Demonstrate the ability to work with different computer programs and databases and software. Demonstrate the ability to present the COM in an appropriate and positive fashion in public meetings, testimony and public appearances. Maintain professional literacy in academic field. Possess excellent oral and written communication skills. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply for this position: Please submit a letter of application, a current curriculum vitae, unofficial copies of transcripts, and the names and email addresses for three references via our online application system: https:www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu. Automated reference requests and a confirmation email will be generated upon submission of your application. Candidates who fail to submit all of the aforementioned material will not be considered. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Committed to excellence through diversity, IUP is an equal opportunity employer M/F/D/V and is a proud member of the State System of Higher Education. All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5363431/college-of-osteopathic-medicine-biomedical-sciences-tenure-track-faculty": {
      "title": "College of Osteopathic Medicine Biomedical Sciences Tenure Track Faculty",
      "description": "College of Osteopathic Medicine Biomedical Sciences Tenure Track Faculty Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02510 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Medicine Opening Date 06/09/2026 Closing Date Continuous Reference Number 2026-6 COM Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description Summary The IUP College of Osteopathic Medicine (COM) invites applicants for a tenure track faculty teaching position in Biomedical Sciences beginning in the Fall of 2026. The faculty will provide support for the organization, development, operationalization, and assessment of the clinically oriented biomedical science aspects of the educational curriculum from year 1 to 4 in the IUP College of Osteopathic Medicine (COM). The faculty member will work closely with the Dean’s Office in the College of Osteopathic Medicine at IUP. Duties Develop and deliver biomedical sciences curriculum with an emphasis on clinically-oriented integration across foundational and systems-based courses Contribute to the design and implementation of course and system-level curricular objectives aligned with programmatic outcomes Participate in the development and teaching of the Foundations course in Year 1 Teach in face-to-face classroom and laboratory settings, including anatomy and related biomedical sciences, as appropriate to expertise Collaborate with faculty across biomedical, clinical, and osteopathic disciplines to support vertical and horizontal curriculum integration in Years 1–2 Contribute to clinically relevant biomedical science content in clinical clerkship syllabi in Years 3–4, as appropriate. Participate in curriculum delivery, assessment, and continuous quality improvement activities as part of the COM’s ongoing assessment program Engage in scholarly activity, research, and professional service consistent with expectations for tenure and promotion, with an emphasis on osteopathic medicine principles and practice Advise and mentor students regarding academic progress, professional development, and career planning Participate in faculty development activities and contribute to the educational mission of the College Demonstrate professionalism, ethical conduct, and collegiality in all academic and institutional responsibilities Perform other duties as assigned in support of the biomedical sciences curriculum and COM mission Other duties as assigned. Position Qualifications Position Qualifications Required Education, Experience and Certification: Terminal degree (i.e.: DO, MD, PhD, PharmD, EdD, DO/PhD or MD/PhD) Minimum three (1) year academic experience as a faculty member at an accredited US allopathic or osteopathic medical school, or other graduate or undergraduate program with proven experience teaching biomedical sciences in an accredited health-sciences or nursing program. Demonstrated excellence as faculty with experience in development of medical curricula and coursework in a clinically related program Additional coursework or degrees with a focus on medical education leadership and/or curriculum pedagogy and/or human anatomy (preferred) Knowledge,Skills,andAbilities: Demonstrate academic leadership, effective communication, and time management skills Team player Demonstrate ability to mentor and motivate peers Demonstrated leadership and productivity in the areas of clinical or professional service and education Good standing with all regulatory and governmental boards and agencies Demonstrated leadership and administrative experience in clinical, professional or educational settings, preferred The department seeks candidates whose teaching, research, or service has prepared them to contribute to our commitment to diversity and inclusion in higher education. Candidates must communicate effectively and perform well during the interview(s). IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5404694/college-of-osteopathic-medicine-psychiatry-temporary-lead-faculty": {
      "title": "College of Osteopathic Medicine -Psychiatry Temporary Lead Faculty",
      "description": "College of Osteopathic Medicine -Psychiatry Temporary Lead Faculty Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 02539 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Medicine Opening Date 08/03/2026 Closing Date Continuous Reference Number COM 2026-10 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The IUP College of Osteopathic Medicine (COM) invites applicants for a part-time temporary faculty teaching position in Psychiatry beginning in the Fall of 2026. The Psychiatry faculty will provide support for the development, operationalization, delivery, and assessment of psychiatry preclinical and clinical education curriculum. They will be directly responsible for curricular teaching, service to the university, scholarly activity, and in some cases, precepting medical students. This faculty member will lead and facilitate skills labs for residents and students at our graduate medical education partner institutions, ensuring hands-on, competency-based learning experiences as needed. They will also design and deliver structured procedural training sessions to enhance resident and student clinical competencies as needed. Essential Duties: Develop curriculum and course/system curricular objectives for coursework in the College of Osteopathic Medicine, with an emphasis on creating mental/behavioral health-psychiatry curricula, and collaboratively integrating psychiatric training throughout preclinical and clinically oriented courses, including linking courses and programmatic objectives Contribute to the planning, development and evaluation of courses and academic programs within IUP and the COM Promote the mission of IUP and the COM to all faculty, staff, students and to the community at large Promote effective working relationships among faculty, staff and students Contribute to the planning, development and evaluation of courses and academic programs within IUP and the COM Carry out lectures, seminars, small group discussion and/or review of clinical assignments and responsibilities effectively Create goals and objectives for each lecture Organize and present in the psychiatry courses and/or small group discussions Prepare examination questions as well as grade a course or portion of course Meet classes according to published schedule Serve as an active member of the department, working closely with the department head to further the department and College mission and vision Work, as needed, with the Assistant Dean of Clinical Affairs and GME on curricular matters Provide service by attending scheduled faculty meetings and by serving on appointed and or elected committees as required Supervise students during authorized and approved patient care events including health fairs, sports physicals, or community outreach programs Assist in development of syllabi, coursework learning objectives and curricula for clinical clerkships Participate in curriculum development, assessment and quality improvement as a part of the COM’s ongoing quality improvement and assessment program Other duties as assigned related to curriculum development related to psychiatry for the 4-year osteopathic medical education program. Other duties as assigned. Position Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: DO/MD degree and Board Certification in Psychiatry by ABMS or AOA Able to be licensed in Pennsylvania as a physician within the first year of hire date A minimum of 1 year experience teaching at an accredited US osteopathic or allopathic medical school preclinical or clinical medical student setting teaching setting, or ACGME residency program with proven experience in teaching. Academic rank will be commensurate with training and experience. Essential Functions Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Demonstrate academic leadership, effective communication, and time management skills Team player Demonstrate ability to mentor and motivate peers Demonstrated leadership and productivity in the areas of clinical or professional service and education Good standing with all regulatory and governmental boards and agencies Demonstrated leadership and administrative experience in clinical, professional or educational settings, preferred IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5404817/com-temporary-part-time-neuromusculoskeletal-medicine-and-osteopathic-principle": {
      "title": "COM - Temporary Part Time Neuromusculoskeletal Medicine and Osteopathic Principles and Practices",
      "description": "COM - Temporary Part Time Neuromusculoskeletal Medicine and Osteopathic Principles and Practices Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 02540 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Medicine Opening Date 08/03/2026 Closing Date Continuous Reference Number COM 2026-11 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The IUP College of Osteopathic Medicine (COM) invites applicants for a part-time temporary faculty teaching position in Neuromusculoskeletal Medicine and Osteopathic Principles and Practices (NMM/OPP) beginning in the Fall of 2026. Faculty members in the Department of Neuromusculoskeletal Medicine (NMM) support the Chair and work on the development, delivery, and assessment of the longitudinal 4-year OPP/NMM curriculum (including osteopathic integration), as well as teach hands-on in the NMM/OPP department both on campus and at the clinical sites, as well as the primary care department, as appropriate. Faculty will support the development of research and scholarly activity related to Neuromusculoskeletal Medicine (NMM) and be involved in service to the University. Essential Duties: Develop curriculum and course/system curricular objectives for coursework in the proposed COM, with an emphasis on integrating core NMM/OPP related content into clinically oriented courses, including linking course and programmatic objectives Develop the curriculum for the NMM/OPP longitudinal coursework throughout all 4-years of the COM curriculum Coordinate the integration of NMM/OPP related content into clinical system courses in Years 1-2 and clinical clerkship syllabi in Years 3-4 Develop, deliver, integrate, and implement COM pre-clinical NMM/OPP curriculum and student assessment measures including assisting the Chair of Primary Care with the standardized patient and simulated patient encounter programs housed within the Clinical Skills curriculum Assists the Chair in planning, developing, and evaluating the NMM curriculum in years 1-4, as assigned Participates in the instruction and supervision of medical students at all phases of training including didactics, small groups, clinical cases, clinical and NMM skill labs, clinical patient care, simulation training, procedure, task training, and standardized patient encounters Mentors and advise students Assist in development of syllabi, coursework learning objectives and curricula for clinical clerkships, integrating NMM/OPP into each of the clinical disciplines Contributes to the planning, development, and evaluation of courses and the academic program as a whole and integrating NMM/OPP into systems courses, and clinical rotations Assists the Chair in leading Department meetings Meets regularly with the Primary Care Department Chair, the Associate Dean of Preclinical Affairs, and the Associate Dean for Clinical Affairs and GME to provide updates on the NMM curriculum and longitudinal needs in other areas of the University Support in planning and delivering ongoing faculty development activities based on curricular interests and expertise Participate in curriculum development, delivery, assessment and quality improvement as a part of the COM’s ongoing quality improvement and assessment program Demonstrate the highest standards of professionalism and ethical behavior in all aspects of personal and professional actions and performance Demonstrate and role model an ongoing ability to work cooperatively with colleagues, supervisors and support staff Other duties as assigned related to curriculum development related to NMM/OPP for the 4-year osteopathic medical education program Other duties as assigned Position Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Terminal degree DO or MD Minimum 1 year experience teaching at either an accredited US osteopathic medical school preclinical or clinical medical student setting teaching setting, or ACGME residency program with proven experience in teaching OMM/OPP/NMM Current active and unrestricted medical licensure; record free of past disciplinary actions against the medical license IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5453587/utility-plant-operator-2": {
      "title": "Utility Plant Operator 2",
      "description": "Utility Plant Operator 2 Salary $44,273.00 Annually Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02581 Division Administration and Finance Department Cogeneration Plant Opening Date 08/19/2026 Closing Date 10/21/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number AF 2029-19 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description THIS POSITION IS POSTED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE AFSCME COLLECTIVE BARGAINING UNIT SUMMARY: Indiana University of Pennsylvania is seeking qualified candidates to fill a Utility Plant Operator 2 position at it's S.W. Jack Cogeneration Plant. The plant is a 24 simple cycle cogeneration facility that utilizes reciprocating engines and waste heat recovery boilers for electrical and thermal energy production. The successful candidate must be able to work independently on all shift rotations as well as have the ability to respond to any cogent plant emergency in a manner that assures safe and efficient operation of the plant. The Utility Plant Operator 2 performs mechanical or lead work in the operation, maintenance, and repair of boilers, generators, engines and related plant equipment. Position is responsible for the start, and operation of Cogen electrical generating equipment. General supervision is received from the Plant Manager or other technical supervisors who review work for compliance with instructions, procedures, and safe operations. Review the PA Specifications for this Job Title. The above duties are normal for this position. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the classification if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment for this classification. Other duties may be required and assigned. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Carries out sole shift responsibility for utility plant operations. Functions as a lead worker over semi-skilled utility plant staff. Performs skilled maintenance and repair work, such as repairing or replacing boiler tubes and tube bundles, plates, grates, gaskets, safety and steam valves, stokers, feed water pumps, water softeners, and fuel handling and related boiler equipment. Performs skilled maintenance and repair work, such as cleaning and plugging chiller tubes, repairing or replacing chiller barrel gaskets, safety and isolation valves, make-up water pumps, chemical treatment equipment, and related chiller equipment. Distributes and interprets work assignments, demonstrates proper work methods, provides assistance, and reviews work of lower-level utility plant staff for adherence to standards. Operates, maintains, and repairs boilers, generators, engines, auxiliary equipment in accordance with established policies and procedures. Reads gauges, meters, chart recorders, data loggers, and other indicators used to monitor boiler and chiller plant systems; and takes needed action to prevent potential problems. Records data on plant operations, equipment maintenance, personnel attendance, and meter and gauge readings and reports required information to supervisor. Keeps records for an assigned shift of steam, chilled water, or electricity produced, and fuel or water consumed. Adjusts and repairs to boilers, chillers, pumps, and auxiliary equipment. Repairs and re-rolls tubes, and repairs tube bundles. Conducts monthly load bank tests on the Emergency Power Supply System (EPSS) to ensure proper operation. Replaces pump seals, valves, and fittings. Monitors feed and makeup water, tests samples to determine the type and number of inhibitors needed to control impurities, and adds inhibitors as needed. Operates and maintains chillers and performs maintenance and repair on cooling towers. Communicates critical operating information to utility plant staff assigned to the following shift. Performs preventive maintenance and cleans the utility plant equipment and areas in accordance with procedures. Conducts safety tests and verifies operation of safety devices. Paints, cleans, rebuilds, and replaces all operating parts of boilers for annual inspections. Recommends changes in utility plant operating procedures to increase operating efficiency. Operates steam or electric motor-driven fans, pumps, and other related equipment. Unloads and receives deliveries for the plant and places materials in designated storage areas. An employee in this job participates in the performance of other trades’ tasks consistent with operational and organizational requirements. Performs related work as required. WORK SCHEDULE: Three Shift Rotations: 6:30AM-2:30PM 2:30PM-10:30PM 10:30PM-6:30AM * Rotations include weekends and holidays. Position Qualifications MINIMUM EDUCATION AND TRAINING: One year of experience as a Utility Plant Operator 1 (commonwealth title). or One year of semi-skilled work experience in the operation, maintenance, or repair of industrial, commercial, or institutional utility plant systems and related equipment. or An equivalent combination of experience and training that includes six months of semi-skilled work experience in the operation, maintenance, or repair of industrial, commercial, or institutional utility plant systems and related equipment. SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS: Must complete and pass a Pennsylvania Class C Underground Storage Tank Operator course REQUIRED SKILLS AND KNOWLEDGE: Candidates must communicate effectively and perform well in the interview(s). Candidates must have communication skills and cross-cultural abilities to maximize their effectiveness with diverse groups of students, colleagues, and community members. The salary for this position is determined by the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. This position is considered an essential employee as defined by the AFSCME Council 13 Master Agreement, Appendix R. Essential employees are personnel specifically designated by Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) whose presence at work is mandatory to maintain critical operations, safety, care, or facility protection during emergency situations, severe weather events, or official office closings. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for AFSCME employees, please click on the link below: pebtf-summary.pdf (passhe.edu) 01 Do you have one year of experience as a Utility Plant Operator 1 (commonwealth title) or one year of semi-skilled work experience in the operation, maintenance, or repair of industrial, commercial, or institutional utility plant systems and related equipment or an equivalent combination of experience and training that includes six months of semi-skilled work experience in the operation, maintenance, or repair of industrial, commercial, or institutional utility plant systems and related equipment? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/2086799/emergency-service": {
      "title": "Emergency Service",
      "description": "Emergency Service Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 01034 Division Academic Affairs Department Rural Health & Safety Opening Date 05/21/2018 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description Summary EMS Instructor: The position reports to the director of the IRHS. In this position, you will instruct programs in area of responsibility which include Emergency Medical Services, American Heart Association Courses, industrial response medical. Programs include, but are not limited to grant funded and specially contracted courses, as well as training programs at satellite locations. Instructor is expected to maintain all professional credentials required of the position. Instructor is required to serve as a classroom instructor for programs in area of responsibility. As the primary instructor for these programs, the instructor is required to perform all tasks associated with responsibilities in areas of class preparation, conduct, student attendance records, test development and proctoring, student advisement and evaluation. The instructor will be required to perform other tasks as required/requested in support of the Institute for Rural Health and Safety, the College of Health and Human Services and the University. Duties EMS Instructor: To teach EMS Courses for the Institute. Position Qualifications Required Qualifications EMS Instructor: Required Qualifications will vary on course being taught. Verified experience as an emergency services provider in the items below or equivalent combination of education, experience and certification: Pennsylvania Department of Health Emergency Medical Service - Instructor and/or Professional Certificate to practice the \"art of teaching\" and render professional service in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania PA Department of Health Emergency Medical Technician CPR (Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation) and First Aid Instructor (American Heart Association) Preferred Qualifications Other desirable qualifications Associate Degree Bachelor's Degree Master's Degree PA Department of Health – Advanced Emergency Medical Technician Pennsylvania Department of Health Paramedic Pre-hospital RN (PHRN) Physician Assistant (PA-C) Medical Doctor (MD) Advanced Cardiac Life Support (American Heart Association) Pediatric Advanced Life Support (American Heart Association) Pre-Hospital Trauma Life Support (PHTLS) Essential Functions The work of this position occurs in a typical office environment. Although infrequent, periods of heavy exertion may occur. Incumbent must have the following abilities: Ability to travel to field locations and meeting/training sites by motor vehicle when required. Communicate both orally and in writing to issue, receive and carry out instructions and orders effectively and to convey information to a variety of co-workers and the general public. Use a variety of common office machines such as telephones, calculators, copiers, computer terminals, keyboards, video display terminals, auxiliary printers and similar equipment. Employee must be able to observe and react to hazard warnings, backup alarms, flashing lights, voice commands and hand signals. Perform manual duties such as lifting and carrying various weight limits. Operate office equipment which may require stooping, kneeling, bending, stretching and prolonged standing. Provide assistance and guidance to internal and external customers. Follow oral and written instructions. Lift and carry - 25 to 50lbs, push and pull 25 to 50lbs, able to reach above/below shoulder, able to climb ladders, able to kneel, activities occur both indoors/outdoors. Operate passenger vehicles. Special Instructions to Applicants All applicants must submit a cover letter, resume, and an EMT or Paramedic Certification as an attachment via this online application system at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu. Names and email addresses of three references must be provided as part of the job application. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Application review will continue until all positions are filled. You will receive a confirmation email when your application has been successfully submitted. Please do not fax, mail or e-mail any documentation. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon confirmation of work eligibility and satisfactory completion of all pre-employment background checks. Committed to excellence through diversity, IUP is an equal opportunity employer M/F/H/V and is a proud member of the State System of Higher Education. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. Non-mgmt, non-represented employees 01 Please provide the name, relationship and contact telephone (with area code) for three (3) references in the box below. [Please do not list any family members.] Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/2763552/non-credit-lecturer-criminal-justice-training-center-school-security-person": {
      "title": "Non-Credit Lecturer - Criminal Justice & Training Center - School Security Personnel Instructor",
      "description": "Non-Credit Lecturer - Criminal Justice & Training Center - School Security Personnel Instructor Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 01477 Division Academic Affairs Department Criminal Justice Training Center Opening Date 04/10/2020 Reference Number 9999 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The Criminal Justice Training Center in the College of Health and Human Services at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applications for School Security Personnel Instructors. Enacted in July of 2019, Act 67 defines and delineates training requirements for School Resource Officers (SROs), School Police Officers (SPOs), and School Security Officers (SSOs) according to standards established by the Pennsylvania Commission on Crime and Delinquency. The position reports to the Director of the Criminal Justice Training Center. In this position, you will instruct best practices in areas of responsibility designed for law enforcement officers, school security officers, and/or administrators working within a school setting. School-based topics include Special Education, cultural diversity, school law, physical security and emergency operations, trauma informed care practices, mentoring students, instructional techniques, social media, drug trends, threat assessment and more. Classes may be online, in person at the CJTC, or a satellite location. The instructor is required to perform all tasks associated with responsibilities in areas of class preparation, conduct, student attendance records, test development and proctoring, student advisement and evaluation. The instructor will be required to perform other tasks as required/requested in support of the Criminal Justice Training Center and the University. Position Qualifications Required : Must have a 4-year college degree from an accredited college or university, or equivalent experience. Minimum of five (5) years of law enforcement experience or as a school administrator, post-secondary teaching experience, or specialized certification in discipline areas related to one of the blocks of instruction. Knowledge of school safety/security requirements and programs, knowledge of programs to help at-risk students succeed, and knowledge of school-based policing best practices. Knowledge of adult learning principles, course development, classroom and practical instructional presentation methods, and methods for evaluating training effectiveness. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications (Word, Excel, Publisher, PowerPoint, Outlook), the Internet, and basic audio/visual equipment. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Be willing to complete a qualifying instructor process. Preferred : (3) three years' experience as an instructor teaching police officers or PA State Police MPOETC Basic Instructor Development Certification. Served as the School Resource Officer (SRO) or School Police Officer at any K-12 public school district in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, or at any private school in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania for a period of 5 years. Essential Functions The work of this position occurs in a typical office environment. Although infrequent, periods of heavy exertion may occur. Incumbent must have the following abilities: Ability to travel to field locations and meeting/training sites by motor vehicle when required. Communicate both orally and in writing to issue, receive and carry out instructions and orders effectively and to convey information to a variety of co-workers and the general public. Use a variety of common office machines such as telephones, calculators, copiers, computer terminals, keyboards, video display terminals, auxiliary printers and similar equipment. Employee must be able to observe and react to hazard warnings, backup alarms, flashing lights, voice commands and hand signals. Perform manual duties such as lifting and carrying various weight limits. Operate office equipment which may require stooping, kneeling, bending, stretching and prolonged standing. Provide assistance and guidance to internal and external customers. Follow oral and written instructions. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply for this position , please submit a letter of application, a current curriculum vitae, and unofficial copies of transcripts via our online application system: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu . If the degree listed as required for this position was earned at IUP - no official transcripts are required to be submitted as part of this employment application. IUP HR will verify IUP obtained degrees and only request official transcripts from candidates if needed. Official transcripts will be required prior to hire date for applicants who did not earn the required degrees at IUP. Committed to excellence through diversity, IUP is an equal opportunity employer M/F/D/V and is a proud member of the State System of Higher Education. All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. Non-mgmt, non-represented employees Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/4116035/non-credit-instructor-iup-community-music-school-internal-candidates-only": {
      "title": "Non-Credit Instructor - IUP Community Music School - Internal Candidates Only",
      "description": "Non-Credit Instructor - IUP Community Music School - Internal Candidates Only Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 01996 Division Academic Affairs Department Music, Theatre, and Dance Opening Date 07/26/2023 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The IUP Community Music School (IUPCMS) seeks part-time music instructors to one, provide in person non-credit private music lessons to a student of any age enrolled in the year-round program of the IUPCMS, or two, lead a music ensemble as its director. Per hour renumeration dependent upon music credentials and experience. Position Qualifications Required: Recommendation in writing by a current IUP music professor or equivalent directly to IUPCMS Director that the individual is qualified to provide music lessons on a specific instrument. Must be a music major if applying for Teaching Apprentice level instructor, or hold a bachelors or masters degree in music if applying for Teaching Artist level instructor. If an interview is required, candidates must communicate effectively and perform well during the interview(s). Essential Functions Must be able to provide effective one-on-one private lesson instruction on approved instrument. Must be able to use online software utilized to run the IUPCMS, to include accurately logging/marking all lessons. Timely and thorough communication, primarily through email, is also essential for success. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply for this position , please request a recommendation be submitted by email to the director of the IUPCMS at jwacker@iup.edu by an IUP music professor or equivalent. Any candidate who does not have a recommendation on file with the IUPCMS Director will not be considered. Committed to excellence through diversity, IUP is an equal opportunity employer M/F/D/V and is a proud member of the State System of Higher Education. All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. Non-mgmt, non-represented employees Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5513495/art-design-temporary-faculty-spring-2027": {
      "title": "Art & Design Temporary Faculty Spring 2027",
      "description": "Art & Design Temporary Faculty Spring 2027 Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 02609 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 10/21/2026 Closing Date 11/21/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number ST2027 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The Department of Art and Design at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applicants for anticipated part-time, temporary faculty position(s) in Studio Art for the Spring 2027 semester. The department seeks candidates whose teaching, research, and/or service has prepared them to contribute to IUP’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in higher education. Teaching: Successful candidates must be able to teach undergraduate courses (face-to-face/hybrid). May also include work at the Punxsutawney Campus. Potential courses include: ART 114 – Color and Two Dimensional Design Focuses on the consistent properties of color and the manner in which two-dimensional design can be organized. Gives specific attention to the complex interactions of color within two-dimensional design. Other duties involve participating in departmental committees and advising students. The successful candidate may be asked to work at off-campus sites and/or provide instruction through distance education asynchronously and/or synchronously through zoom technology. Position Qualifications Required: • Master’s degree in Studio Art or related field. • Experience teaching in college setting. • Experience working with students from underserved backgrounds. • Experience working with underprepared students. • Successful candidates must have the following competencies: comprehensive knowledge of contemporary art and design A portfolio that demonstrates evidence of mastery of color and 2D Design skills Essential Functions Faculty must be able to: Submit required evaluation documentation, including teaching observation materials and course syllabi, in accordance with departmental and university requirements. Teach courses assigned by the Dean on a schedule made of a combination of standard class-meeting times as determined to meet instructional needs and adhere to the requirements of the department's curriculum. Teach courses for a mandated number of contact hours per week over a full semester and meet university expectations for student consultation hours and final exams. Present course material in a clear and organized manner using methodologies appropriate to the discipline. Evaluate student work fairly and promptly. Perform the physical requirements of laboratory, field work, studio work, or other activities outside typical classroom instruction if applicable. Hold regular office hours in accordance with university and departmental requirements. Maintain current knowledge of the discipline through continued scholarly activity and research. Participate actively in assignments necessary to advance the service and/or outreach of the department, college, and university. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf 01 Do you have a portfolio that demonstrates evidence of mastery of color and 2D Design skills Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5513641/art-design-gallery-director-spring-2027": {
      "title": "Art & Design Gallery Director Spring 2027",
      "description": "Art & Design Gallery Director Spring 2027 Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 02610 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 10/21/2026 Closing Date 11/21/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number SpringTemp27 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The Department of Art and Design at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applicants for anticipated part-time, temporary faculty position(s) of Gallery Director for the Spring 2027 semester. The department seeks candidates whose research, and/or service has prepared them to contribute to IUP’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in higher education. The Kipp Gallery director is responsible for installing and maintaining exhibitions in the Kipp and Annex galleries in Sprowls Hall on the campus of IUP. The director will handle all communication with visiting artists for the current academic year and will work with the gallery committee to plan and schedule the galleries for the upcoming year. The gallery director will supervise student workers to assist in gallery installation and maintenance. The gallery director will plan and promote gallery receptions, artist talks, and other related activities. The director will maintain communication with the student co-op, which is the funding source of the gallery, keeping all paperwork up-to-date and in compliance. The gallery director will manage the gallery budget and submit the budget for the upcoming academic year. Position Qualifications Required: • A minimum of a master’s degree in visual art discipline or related field. • The ability to be on campus for in-person events all semester. • Experience with art handling and gallery installation. • Organization, communication, and budgeting skills. Essential Functions Perform the physical requirements of laboratory, field work, studio work, or other activities outside typical classroom instruction if applicable. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf 01 Do you have experience with art handling and gallery installation? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5515659/culinary-arts-part-time-temporary-instructor-spring-2027": {
      "title": "Culinary Arts Part-time Temporary Instructor Spring 2027",
      "description": "Culinary Arts Part-time Temporary Instructor Spring 2027 Location IUP at Punxsutawney Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 02612 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 10/27/2026 Closing Date 11/27/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number CASPTemp2027 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description University of Pennsylvania's Academy of Culinary Arts is seeking a part-time, temporary instructor (spring semester contract) to begin during the 2027 school year. The assignment is at our Punxsutawney campus teaching culinary arts, baking and pastry arts. Applicants must be competent to teach cooking and baking labs as assigned for the Academy of Culinary Arts program The department seeks candidates whose teaching, research, and/or service has prepared them to contribute to IUP’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in higher education. Position Qualifications Required Qualifications: · Graduate of an accredited culinary program. · Have varied industry experience such as fine dining, private club/resort environment, or business ownership. · Ability to demonstrate communication and computer literacy skills. Preferred Qualifications: · Credits earned toward a bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution and/or equivalent industry experience. · Industry experience advancing to supervisory roles as Chef or Pastry Chef. · Teaching experience at the post-secondary or secondary level. Essential Functions Faculty must be able to: Teach courses assigned by the Dean on a schedule made of a combination of standard class-meeting times as determined to meet instructional needs and adhere to the requirements of the department's curriculum. Teach courses for a mandated number of contact hours per week over a full semester and meet university expectations for student consultation hours and final exams. Present course material in a clear and organized manner using methodologies appropriate to the discipline. Evaluate student work fairly and promptly. Perform the physical requirements of laboratory, field work, studio work, or other activities outside typical classroom instruction if applicable. Maintain current knowledge of the discipline through continued scholarly activity and research. Participate actively in assignments necessary to advance the service and/or outreach of the department, college, and university. Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates must submit all required documents successfully and complete the interview process, which may include a classroom demonstration and cooking presentation. The start date for the position will be discussed/determined with applicants participating in the interview process IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5518555/music-theatre-and-dance-temporary-part-time-faculty-spring-2027": {
      "title": "Music, Theatre and Dance Temporary Part Time Faculty Spring 2027",
      "description": "Music, Theatre and Dance Temporary Part Time Faculty Spring 2027 Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 02613 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 10/21/2026 Closing Date 11/21/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number MTDSP2027 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The Department of Music, Theatre and Dance at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applicants for anticipated part-time, temporary faculty position(s) for the Spring 2027 semester. The department seeks candidates whose teaching, research, and/or service have prepared them to serve all IUP students. Teaching: Successful candidates must be able to teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses offered in person, online or through distance education, or at one of our other locations. Courses may include: Thea221 Performance Lighting Introduces concepts and develops skills to apply lighting technology to various stage, video and photographed performances. Acquire skills in instrument selection, system set up, and console programming. Develop beginning level practices of lighting composition, lighting color theory, and cueing. Practice of competencies required by corequisite enrollment in THEA 486 for .5 credits. Thea486 Practicum in Production: Lighting and Sound Develop skills through artistic practice of performance, production, dramaturgy and applied theatre. Engage with faculty led, professionally modeled productions of plays, musicals and dance. Increase competency in acting, directing, stage management, design/technology, dramaturgical research and applied theatre techniques including simulation practices. THEA 486 Practicum includes faculty design work in Lighting and/or Sound, or the direct supervision of student Lighting and Sound Designers for productions of Antigone and Antigone, Presented by the Girl’s of St. Catherine’s with performance dates in April. Responsibilities Other duties involve participating in departmental committees and advising students. The successful candidate may be asked to work at off-campus sites and/or provide instruction through distance education asynchronously and/or synchronously through zoom technology. Position Qualifications Required: • Terminal degree in Theatre or related field, OR Master’s degree with 7+ years of related professional experience in the discipline. • Experience teaching in college setting. Essential Functions Faculty members are expected to: Teach courses assigned by the department chair in accordance with departmental, college, and university scheduling requirements. Conduct classes for the required contact hours each academic term and administer final examinations or equivalent assessments as required. Present course content effectively using instructional methods appropriate to the discipline and learning objectives. Evaluate student performance accurately, fairly, and in a timely manner. Perform activities associated with laboratory instruction, fieldwork, studio courses, clinical assignments, or other experiential learning environments, when applicable. Maintain expertise in the discipline through ongoing scholarly, research, creative, and/or professional activities. Engage in service activities that support the department, college, university, profession, and community, as appropriate. Communicate effectively with students, colleagues, and external stakeholders in both written and oral formats. Adhere to university policies, academic standards, and professional expectations. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5524012/social-studies-education-temporary-faculty-spring-2027": {
      "title": "Social Studies Education -Temporary Faculty Spring 2027",
      "description": "Social Studies Education -Temporary Faculty Spring 2027 Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 02614 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 10/27/2026 Closing Date 11/27/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number AA-26 StudTch Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The College of Education and Human Services at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applicants for anticipated part-time, temporary faculty position(s) as Assistant Student Teaching Supervisor for the Spring 2027 semester. The Assistant Student Teaching Supervisor supports the Secondary Social Studies Education Program in supervising teacher candidates enrolled in EDUC 441. Working under the direction of the program coordinator and university supervisor, the individual assists with classroom observations, instructional feedback, candidate mentoring, and communication with cooperating teachers to ensure a successful student-teaching experience. The department seeks candidates whose teaching, research, and/or service has prepared them to contribute to IUP’s commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in higher education. Teaching: Successful candidates must be able to teach undergraduate courses (face-to-face/hybrid). May also include work at the Punxsutawney Campus. Potential courses include: EDUC 441 An experience in teaching at the elementary or secondary level; coordination and visitation by a university faculty member with daily supervision by a cooperating classroom teacher. Primary Responsibilities Classroom Observation and Evaluation Conduct scheduled observations of student teachers in their assigned middle and high school classrooms. Evaluate instructional planning, lesson delivery, classroom management, student engagement, and assessment practices. Provide constructive written and verbal feedback to support professional growth. Assist with midterm and final evaluations using established university assessment instruments. Student Teacher Mentoring Support teacher candidates in developing effective instructional strategies and classroom management techniques. Provide guidance on lesson planning, instructional differentiation, assessment, and professional responsibilities. Assist candidates in identifying areas for improvement and developing strategies to address them. Coordination with Cooperating Teachers Maintain regular communication with cooperating teachers regarding candidate performance and progress. Participate in conferences involving student teachers, cooperating teachers, and university supervisors. Help identify and resolve concerns related to candidate performance or placement. Documentation and Program Support Maintain records of classroom observations, feedback, and candidate progress. Assist with the completion of required student-teaching assessments and documentation. Communicate concerns requiring additional intervention to the program coordinator. Support compliance with university policies and Pennsylvania Department of Education requirements. Other duties involve participating in departmental committees and advising students. The successful candidate may be asked to work at off-campus sites and/or provide instruction through distance education asynchronously and/or synchronously through zoom technology. Position Qualifications Required Terminal degree in Education or related field, OR Master’s degree with 3+ years of related professional experience in Education. Experience mentoring student teachers and supervising classroom instruction. Preferred Experience supervising university students teaching at the secondary level. Familiarity with Pennsylvania academic standards, instructional assessment, and teacher certification requirements. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Essential Functions Faculty must be able to: Teach courses assigned by the Dean on a schedule made of a combination of standard class-meeting times as determined to meet instructional needs and adhere to the requirements of the department's curriculum. Teach courses for a mandated number of contact hours per week over a full semester and meet university expectations for student consultation hours and final exams. Present course material in a clear and organized manner using methodologies appropriate to the discipline. Evaluate student work fairly and promptly. Perform the physical requirements of laboratory, field work, studio work, or other activities outside typical classroom instruction if applicable. Maintain current knowledge of the discipline through continued scholarly activity and research. Participate actively in assignments necessary to advance the service and/or outreach of the department, college, and university. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf 01 Do you have a degree in education or a related discipline? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5526941/music-history-temporary-faculty-spring-2027": {
      "title": "Music History Temporary Faculty Spring 2027",
      "description": "Music History Temporary Faculty Spring 2027 Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Part Time and Temporary Job Number 02615 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 10/27/2026 Closing Date 11/27/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number MHSP2027 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The Department of Music, Theatre, and Dance at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applicants for an anticipated part-time, temporary faculty position for the Spring 2027 semester. The department serves approximately 130 undergraduate and graduate music majors in the BA, BFA Performance, BSEd Music Education, and MA in Music degrees. The department seeks candidates whose teaching, research, and/or service have prepared them to serve all IUP students. Teaching: Successful candidates must be able to teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses offered in person, online or through distance education, or at on of our other locations. The anticipated course load is: MUHI 302, Music History II (two sections): Examines selected musicians, music cultures, aesthetic directions, and repertoires of Europe and the Americas from the late 18th century to the present, as well as influential musical traditions from Asia and Africa, via a case studies approach. Develops research writing skills in musicology, as well as the ability to synthesize connections between diverse spheres of musical activity. Responsibilities: Other duties involve participating in departmental committees. The successful candidate may be asked to work at off-campus sites and/or provide instruction through distance education asynchronously and/or synchronously through zoom technology. Position Qualifications Required: • Terminal degree in the music/music history or related field, OR Master’s degree with 3+ years of related professional experience in the music/music history. • Experience teaching music history or related disciplines in college setting. Essential Functions Faculty members are expected to: Teach courses assigned by the department chair in accordance with departmental, college, and university scheduling requirements. Conduct classes for the required contact hours each academic term and administer final examinations or equivalent assessments as required. Present course content effectively using instructional methods appropriate to the discipline and learning objectives. Evaluate student performance accurately, fairly, and in a timely manner. Perform activities associated with laboratory instruction, fieldwork, studio courses, clinical assignments, or other experiential learning environments, when applicable. Maintain expertise in the discipline through ongoing scholarly, research, creative, and/or professional activities. Engage in service activities that support the department, college, university, profession, and community, as appropriate. Communicate effectively with students, colleagues, and external stakeholders in both written and oral formats. Adhere to university policies, academic standards, and professional expectations. Special Instructions to Applicants Applications for this position must be submitted via our online application system at www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu and must be received by December 1, 2027. IUP accepts online applications only - mailed, faxed or emailed applications will not be accepted. A complete application will consist of: 1. a letter of application; 2. a current curriculum vitae; 3. unofficial copies of transcripts; and 4. names and email addresses of three professional references. Only complete applications will be considered. Review of applications will continue until position is filled. Successful applicants will be required to provide official transcripts from all colleges and universities within 10 days of the date of hire. Automated reference requests will be generated when application is submitted by applicant. Reference requests from outside the U.S. must be submitted directly to the Office of Human Resources, human-resources@iup.edu. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5527409/the-counseling-center-tenure-track-faculty": {
      "title": "The Counseling Center - Tenure Track Faculty",
      "description": "The Counseling Center - Tenure Track Faculty Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02616 Division Student Affairs Opening Date 10/27/2026 Closing Date 11/27/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number 2025-22 SA Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description The Counseling Center at Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) invites applications for a permanent, tenure-track faculty position beginning August 2027. The Psychologist/Counselor will provide a variety of counseling and/or psychological services to IUP undergraduate and graduate students. This is a 9-month position. Duties: • Faculty provide intake, triage, individual and group counseling for undergraduate and graduate students. • Faculty provide outreach/consultation for the IUP community, and crisis intervention services for IUP students. • In addition, faculty members serve on departmental and university committees, maintain licensure, and engage in scholarly activities. Understanding of marginalization, social inequity, prejudice, and discrimination are essential. • Faculty rotate daytime on-call responsibilities. • Faculty members have the opportunity to supervise graduate trainees in IUP’s doctoral programs in Clinical Psychology and/or Counselor Education and Supervision. Position Qualifications Required: Doctorate degree in Clinical Psychology, Counseling Psychology or a closely related field by August 2027 required. Currently licensed or license- eligible (within two years of appointment) in Pennsylvania required. Preferred: University/College counseling center experience is preferred. Essential Functions Non-teaching faculty must have, and maintain the physical and mental abilities, communicative skills, and stamina necessary to carry out the essential functions of their positions. Work involves sitting most of the time, but may involve standing to a significant degree, walking for brief periods of time and may include driving requirements. Must be able to: Maintain current knowledge of the discipline through continued scholarly activity and research. Participate actively in assignments necessary to advance the service and/or outreach of the department, college, and university. Ability to travel to field locations and meeting/training sites by motor vehicle when required. Communicate both orally and in writing to issue, receive and carry out instructions and orders effectively and to convey information to a variety of co-workers and the general public. Use a variety of common office machines such as telephones, calculators, copiers, computer terminals, keyboards, video display terminals, auxiliary printers, and similar equipment. Employee must be able to observe and react to hazard warnings, backup alarms, flashing lights, voice commands and hand signals. Operate office equipment which may require stooping, kneeling, bending, stretching and prolonged standing. Provide assistance and guidance to internal and external customers. Follow oral and written instructions. Special Instructions to Applicants FAXED DOCUMENTATION WILL NOT BE ACCEPTED. All other applicants: Please submit a letter of application addressing professional skills, a current curriculum vitae, graduate transcripts, and three letters of reference addressing the applicant's expertise in college counseling/therapy (confidential links will be sent to the recommenders provided in the application upon submission) via our online application system: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu . Automated reference requests and a confirmation email will be generated upon submission of your application. Candidates who fail to submit all of the aforementioned materials will not be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. If the degree listed as required for this position was earned at IUP - no official transcripts are required to be submitted as part of this employment application. IUP HR will verify IUP obtained degrees and only request official transcripts from candidates if needed. Official transcripts will be required prior to hire date for applicants who did not earn the required degrees at IUP. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for APSCUF employees, please click on the link below: www.passhe.edu/inside/hr/syshr/benefit_highlights/sshe_highlights.pdf 01 Will you have a Doctorate degree in Clinical Psychology, Counseling Psychology or closely related field by August 2027? Yes No 02 Are you currently licensed or license- eligible (within two years of appointment) in Pennsylvania? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5533281/custodial-worker-1": {
      "title": "Custodial Worker 1",
      "description": "Custodial Worker 1 Salary $32,724.00 Annually Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02622 Division Administration and Finance Department Custodial Services Opening Date 10/28/2026 Closing Date 11/7/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number AF 2026-26 Description Benefits Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description THIS POSITION IS POSTED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE AFSCME COLLECTIVE BARGAINING UNIT SUMMARY: This is routine manual work involving the maintenance of cleanliness and safety in state-operated facilities, buildings, and grounds. Employees perform a variety of standard or aseptic cleaning and sanitation tasks and work independently to complete the assigned day-to-day custodial duties. Work is subject to inspection while in progress or upon completion for adherence to established standards of cleanliness. Detailed supervisory guidance and review is provided for new or unusual situations and changes in operating procedures. Review the PA Specifications for this Job Title. The above duties are normal for this position. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the classification if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment for this classification. Other duties may be required and assigned. Essential Duties: Utilize tools and equipment of the custodial trade in the performance of cleaning tasks. Sweep, mop, vacuum, scrub, wax, and buff floors. Clean, dust, and polish furniture and fixtures. Wash and clean windows, walls, and doors. Clean toilets, sinks, and mirrors in restrooms; replace restroom supplies. Gather and dispose of waste products, recyclable materials, infectious waste, and hazardous materials according to safe material handling guidelines. Move furniture and equipment when necessary to perform custodial tasks. Secure and maintain cleaning equipment; request, pick up, and store related supplies. Report needed repairs to crew leader or supervisor. Shovel snow; sweep and clean walkways; assist in keeping immediate outside premises and building entrances in an orderly condition. Perform incidental assignments, such as removing ashes, and making simple repairs. Document work performed. Perform related work as required. WORK SCHEDULE: Monday to Friday 6:00 AM to 2:00 PM Position Qualifications MINIMUM EXPERIENCE AND TRAINING : No previous experience and training required. REQUIRED SKILLS AND KNOWLEDGE: Candidates must communicate effectively and perform well in the interview(s). Candidates must have communication skills and cross-cultural abilities to maximize their effectiveness with diverse groups of students, colleagues, and community members. The salary for this position is determined by the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. This position is considered an essential employee as defined by the AFSCME Council 13 Master Agreement, Appendix R. Essential employees are personnel specifically designated by Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) whose presence at work is mandatory to maintain critical operations, safety, care, or facility protection during emergency situations, severe weather events, or official office closings. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for AFSCME employees, please click on the link below: pebtf-summary.pdf (passhe.edu) Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5533335/custodial-worker-1-shift-preference-internal-bidders-only-first-shift": {
      "title": "Custodial Worker 1 - SHIFT PREFERENCE, INTERNAL BIDDERS ONLY (First Shift)",
      "description": "Custodial Worker 1 - SHIFT PREFERENCE, INTERNAL BIDDERS ONLY (First Shift) Salary $32,724.00 Annually Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02623 Division Administration and Finance Department Custodial Services Opening Date 10/29/2026 Closing Date 11/3/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number AF 2026-29 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description THIS POSITION IS POSTED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE AFSCME COLLECTIVE BARGAINING UNIT SUMMARY: This is routine manual work involving the maintenance of cleanliness and safety in state-operated facilities, buildings, and grounds. Employees perform a variety of standard or aseptic cleaning and sanitation tasks and work independently to complete the assigned day-to-day custodial duties. Work is subject to inspection while in progress or upon completion for adherence to established standards of cleanliness. Detailed supervisory guidance and review is provided for new or unusual situations and changes in operating procedures. Review the PA Specifications for this Job Title. The above duties are normal for this position. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the classification if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment for this classification. Other duties may be required and assigned. Essential Duties: Utilize tools and equipment of the custodial trade in the performance of cleaning tasks. Sweep, mop, vacuum, scrub, wax, and buff floors. Clean, dust, and polish furniture and fixtures. Wash and clean windows, walls, and doors. Clean toilets, sinks, and mirrors in restrooms; replace restroom supplies. Gather and dispose of waste products, recyclable materials, infectious waste, and hazardous materials according to safe material handling guidelines. Move furniture and equipment when necessary to perform custodial tasks. Secure and maintain cleaning equipment; request, pick up, and store related supplies. Report needed repairs to crew leader or supervisor. Shovel snow; sweep and clean walkways; assist in keeping immediate outside premises and building entrances in an orderly condition. Perform incidental assignments, such as removing ashes, and making simple repairs. Document work performed. Perform related work as required. WORK SCHEDULE: Monday through Friday 6:00 AM to 2:00 PM Position Qualifications MINIMUM EXPERIENCE AND TRAINING : No previous experience and training required. REQUIRED SKILLS AND KNOWLEDGE: Candidates must communicate effectively and perform well in the interview(s). Candidates must have communication skills and cross-cultural abilities to maximize their effectiveness with diverse groups of students, colleagues, and community members. The salary for this position is determined by the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. This position is considered an essential employee as defined by the AFSCME Council 13 Master Agreement, Appendix R. Essential employees are personnel specifically designated by Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) whose presence at work is mandatory to maintain critical operations, safety, care, or facility protection during emergency situations, severe weather events, or official office closings. Special Instructions to Applicants This position is posted consistent with the N-1 Bargaining Unit in accordance with the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement notifying: 1. Full-time, regular Custodial Worker 1 employees of an opportunity to submit a bid for shift preference. 2. Full-time temporary Custodial Worker 1 employees of an opportunity to submit a bid for a regular Custodial Worker 1. 3. If no shift or seniority bids are received, this position will be posted for all other applicants for an additional 10 days. Current employees in their probationary period will only be considered for shift preference or seniority bidding within their classification series. Bidders can submit their interest in this position by replying to supplemental questions on the online job application. Bidders are not required to submit a cover letter or resume. Please do not fax, mail or e-mail any documentation. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for AFSCME employees, please click on the link below: pebtf-summary.pdf (passhe.edu) 01 Are you an IUP Employee? Yes No 02 Internal Applicants Only: I am requesting a Custodial Worker 1 Shift Preference/Schedule Change bid for this position. Yes No 03 Are you currently a full-time, regular Custodial Worker 1 or full-time, temporary Custodial Worker 1 submitting bidding rights? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/iupedu/jobs/5533399/administrative-assistant-1-office-of-financial-aid": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant 1 - Office of Financial Aid",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant 1 - Office of Financial Aid Salary $46,827.00 Annually Location Indiana, PA 15701 Job Type Full Time and Regular Job Number 02624 Division Student Affairs Department Financial Aid Opening Date 10/29/2026 Closing Date 11/8/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Reference Number SA 2026-24 Description Benefits Questions Nestled in the scenic foothills of western Pennsylvania, Indiana University of Pennsylvania (IUP) offers more than a place to work—it offers a vibrant campus community where innovation, collaboration, and natural beauty come together. Our picturesque campus features tree-lined walkways, historic architecture, and welcoming green spaces that create an inspiring environment for learning, working, and connecting. At IUP, employees are part of a supportive and engaged community dedicated to student success, academic excellence, and meaningful impact. Located in the charming college town of Indiana, Pennsylvania—just over an hour from Pittsburgh—our campus combines small-town warmth with access to the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities of a major metropolitan area. Whether enjoying a walk across the Oak Grove, collaborating with colleagues in dynamic academic spaces, or engaging in the many cultural and community events hosted throughout the year, IUP offers an exceptional place to build a career and make a difference. Position Summary & Description THIS POSITION IS POSTED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE AFSCME COLLECTIVE BARGAINING UNIT SUMMARY: The Administrative Assistant 1 provides administrative and operational support to the Financial Aid Office. Review the PA Specifications for this Job Title. The above duties are normal for this position. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the classification if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment for this classification. Other duties may be required and assigned. ESSENTIAL DUTIES: Coordinate the hiring, training, and supervision of student employees within the Financial Aid Office. Staff the Financial Aid Service counter. Monitor the financial-aid@iup.edu email account, including responding to and forwarding messages, as appropriate. Respond to incoming phone inquiries from students, parents, and university employees, providing accurate and timely information regarding financial aid programs, processes, and requirements. Proof and upload weekly award letters, Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) appeal forms, scholarship appeals, and other documents to Student Forms via Campus Logic. Run and review weekly reports to identify C-Flags and Aggregate Loan Maximum alerts. Monitor and manage the Financial Aid suspense file, ensuring outstanding items are reviewed and resolved in a timely manner. Review and process University refund advance requests. Order office supplies, equipment, and other necessary items through SourcePoint. Oversee purchasing card transactions and all associated processes and required documentation. Prepare and process landlord letters for students as requested. Submit and coordinate office maintenance requests as needed. Oversee and monitor the Financial Aid Office budget, including tracking expenditures and available funds. Maintain and update the Financial Aid website to ensure information is accurate and current. Review, monitor, and update student waivers, ensuring financial aid and student billing records are accurately aligned. Process requests for cost and financial aid information related to Office of Vocational Rehabilitation (OVR) and outside scholarships. Review and process Will Not Attend and Will Not Return notifications and make necessary financial aid award adjustments. Assist directors with data entry and other projects as assigned. WORK SCHEDULE: Monday through Friday 8:00 AM to 4:30 PM Position Qualifications MINIMUM EDUCATION AND TRAINING: Graduation from an accredited four-year college or university . or An equivalent combination of education, training, and relevant work experience. REQUIRED SKILLS AND KNOWLEDGE: Candidates must communicate effectively and perform well in the interview(s). Candidates must have communication skills and cross-cultural abilities to maximize their effectiveness with diverse groups of students, colleagues, and community members. The salary for this position is determined by the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. IUP is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering an inclusive and welcoming workplace. We do not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. In accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants and employees with disabilities may request reasonable accommodations to participate in the application or interview process or to perform the essential functions of a position. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs, consistent with the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants who require an accommodation during the recruitment process are encouraged to contact human-resources@iup.edu . All offers of employment are contingent upon verification of earned degrees through the receipt of official transcripts, confirmation of work eligibility, and satisfactory completion of background checks. For an overview of IUP benefit information available for AFSCME employees, please click on the link below: pebtf-summary.pdf (passhe.edu) 01 Did you graduate from an accredited four-year college or university, or do you have an equivalent combination of education, training, and relevant work experience? Yes No Required Question Employer Indiana University of Pennsylvania Address 1011 South Drive Sutton Hall Room 360 Indiana, Pennsylvania, 15705 Phone 724-357-2431 Website http://www.iup.edu/employment Apply"
    }
  },
